#. ~ Description of "dragon skin vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A ballistic vest made of disc-shaped ceramic scales arranged in an "
"overlapping pattern, like the scales of a mythical dragon.  The design "
"allows it to absorb many more impacts without becoming fully compromised "
"like a ballistic plate might, but it was never widely adopted due to its "
"failure to meet high-temperature operational tests.  While well past its "
"warranty date, it remains a highly sought after collecter's item."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "soft ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A bulky but comfortable armor vest.  It lacks pockets for ballistic plate "
"inserts, but the IIIa rating on its label suggests that it should stand up "
"to everything short of high-powered rifle rounds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A crudely-hammered piece of sheet metal, wrapped in rags in an attempt to "
"prevent spalling.  If used in a ballistic vest, it might offer some "
"protection."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "scrap ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A flat piece of salvaged steel, crudely cut and bent into the shape of an "
"ESBI ballistic plate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous "
"portion of glue to form an armor plate for the front or back of the torso.  "
"This could be used in a plate carrier in lieu of an ESAPI plate, though it "
"probably won't stand up to much."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous "
"portion of glue to form an armor plate for the front or back of the torso.  "
"This could be used in an oversized plate carrier, though it probably won't "
"stand up to much."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "paper ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A great many layers of paper stacked and laminated together with a generous "
"portion of glue to form an armor plate for the sides of the torso.  This "
"could be used in a plate carrier in lieu of an ESBI plate, though it "
"probably won't stand up to much."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A hand-forged steel ballistic plate more than double the standard size.  It "
"can't be worn on its own, and would need to be inserted into an equally "
"gigantic plate carrier vest to be of any benefit."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A hand-forged steel ballistic plate, designed to be used in a ballistic "
"vest."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty vest with specialized pockets to hold hard armor plates, the "
"sort of thing you see on soldiers and armored car drivers.  A soft kevlar "
"liner provides protection against spalling and low-caliber firearms.  It "
"sports MOLLE webbing for attaching compatable accessories."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "steel ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A hexagonal piece of steel forged into a side insert for a plate carrier and"
" padded with synthetic fabric."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "compromised ceramic front plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A large ballistic plate that has been cracked by damage.  It no longer "
"provides reliable protection, but it's still just as heavy."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa grande de balística que está dañada. Ya no brinda una "
"protección confiable pero sigue siendo gruesa."

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A level II Kevlar vest, rated for low-caliber pistol rounds and designed to "
"be worn under clothing.  Concerningly, it is sized for a toddler."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight ballistic armor vest, suitable for wearing under clothing.  "
"Its level II rating suggests that it should help against lower-caliber "
"pistol rounds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "stab vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight soft armor vest.  The level II rating on the label suggests it"
" will protect from knife attacks and low caliber handguns, provided it has "
"its matching stab plate inserts."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "compromised ceramic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A medium-sized ballistic plate that has been cracked by damage.  It no "
"longer provides reliable protection, but it's still just as heavy."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa mediana de balística que está dañada. Ya no brinda una "
"protección confiable pero sigue siendo gruesa."

#. ~ Description of "deltoid ballistic plates"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A pair of NIJ Level III ballistic plates with a concave profile, made of "
"UHMW polyethylene.  \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  These "
"plates are designed to be worn in the shoulder pockets of suitable plate "
"carriers or combat shirts, and can resist several high-energy rifle rounds "
"before breaking.  Deltoid plates such as these are very infrequently worn "
"due to their marginal utility in improving survivability."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A panel of wood cut into an irregular hexagon, slightly concave.  It would "
"fit in a plate carrier sized for a giant, and while by no means capable of "
"stopping gunfire, it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "ESBI ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of "
"ceramic.  \"STRIKE FACE\" is printed on its outer surface.  This is designed"
" to be worn in the sides of a plate carrier, and can withstand several high-"
"energy rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa poligonal para balística, levemente cóncava, hecha de cerámico."
" Su parte exterior tiene impresa \"STRIKE FACE\". Está diseñada para ser "
"usada en los costados de un porta placas y puede soportar varios impactos de"
" rifle de alta energía antes de romperse."

#. ~ Description of "ESAPI ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A polygonal ballistic plate with a slightly concave profile, made of "
"ceramic.  Its inner surface is coated with UHMW polyethylene and is labeled "
"\"TOP\", while the outer surface is labeled \"STRIKE FACE\".  This is "
"intended to be worn in a ballistic vest, and can withstand several high-"
"energy rifle rounds before breaking."
msgstr ""
"Es una placa poligonal para balística, levemente cóncava y hecha de "
"cerámica. Su superficie interna está recubierta de polietileno UHMW, y está "
"etiquetado como \"TOP\", mientras que su parte exterior dice \"STRIKE "
"FACE\". Está diseñado para ser usado dentro de un chaleco balístico y puede "
"soportar varios impactos de rifle de alta energía antes de romperse."

#. ~ Description of "EOD fragmentation plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A polygonal fragmentation plate with a slightly concave profile, made of "
"thin layers of steel, UHMW polyethylene, foam, and Kevlar.  Though certified"
" to provide protection from fragmentation, it will not provide much "
"protection from firearms.  This is intended to be inserted into an EOD suit,"
" and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "concealable ballistic vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A preposterously sized Kevlar vest faced with ballistic nylon  Its low-"
"profile design is perfect for wearing under clothing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic side plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of wood cut into a small irregular hexagon.  It would fit in the "
"side pockets of a plate carrier, and while by no means capable of stopping "
"gunfire, it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wooden ballistic plate"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of wood cut into an irregular hexagon, slightly concave.  It would "
"fit in a plate carrier, and while by no means capable of stopping gunfire, "
"it may still hold up against other threats."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "half plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A simple plate carrier vest covering just the upper torso, with a soft "
"kevlar liner and a front and back pockets for armor plates to keep your "
"organs from being perforated by small-arms fire.  It features a MOLLE "
"cummerbund that you can tuck a few magazines into."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "lightweight plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A slimmed-down kevlar vest with inserts for hard ballistic armor plates in "
"front and back.  It offers plenty of protection without any accessories or "
"extra bits to get in the way."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "soft stab panel"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A soft armor insert designed to protect against stab wounds.  This is "
"intended to be inserted into a ballistic vest, and can't be worn on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "EOD jacket"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"A thick armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for"
" use by explosive ordnance disposal technicians.  It features a central "
"pocket for a large plate, and near complete coverage in fragmentation "
"resistant materials.  Aside from the plate, it offers insufficient "
"protection from ballistic threats."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "tactical EOD jacket"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"An armored jacket constructed from Kevlar, Nomex, and foam padding, for use "
"by explosive ordnance disposal technicians in 'non-permissive environments'."
"  It is lighter than normal EOD armor to allow for wearing a plate carrier "
"beneath it.  It features two pockets in the arms covering the deltoids for "
"additional optional protection."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "plate carrier"
#: data/json/items/armor/ballistic_armor.json
msgid ""
"An enormous handmade ballistic vest with MOLLE webbing for attaching "
"accessories.  No factory ever made ESAPI plates that would fit in this "
"thing, but it ought to be possible to make some out of steel or other "
"materials."
msgstr ""

