#. ~ Description of "wool coif"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A cloth coif with neck and forehead protection.  Resting on your shoulders, "
"it serves as padding for a helmet.  Though it's pretty warm, it is "
"constructed of layered wool quilting and provides substantial protection "
"even on its own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted arming pants"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A facsimile of padded armor once used in the middle ages, these pants are "
"made of quilted fabric filled with dense stuffing.  Though the design is "
"centuries old, it looks like their time may have come round again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted gambeson (loose)"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval coat of quilted armor made of a few layers of durable cloth with "
"stuffing sewn in between.  These versatile garments could serve as "
"protection on their own, or be used as part of a set, with mail or leather "
"worn beneath.  Activate it to tighten the fit."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted gambeson"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval jacket of quilted armor made of a few layers of durable cloth "
"with stuffing sewn in between.  These versatile garments could serve as "
"protection on their own, or be used as part of a set, with mail or leather "
"worn on the outer layers.  Activate it to loosen the ties and wear it as "
"outerwear instead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted coif"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval-style head covering made of quilted fabric padded with stuffing."
"  It offers some protection on its own, and might also serve as padding for "
"a proper helmet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted surcoat (loose)"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A simple vest of medieval padded armor, made by sewing stuffing between "
"quilted fabric.  It can serve as standalone protection or be worn over other"
" armor.  Activate it to tighten the fit."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "quilted surcoat"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A simple vest of medieval padded armor, made by sewing stuffing between "
"quilted fabric.  It can serve as standalone protection or be worn under "
"armor.  Activate it to loosen its fit."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool aketon"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A thick cloth jack, intended to be worn below metal armor.  This one is made"
" of layered wool quilting and it provides fairly decent protection on its "
"own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool aketon vest"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"A thick cloth vest, intended to be worn below metal armor.  This one is made"
" of layered wool quilting and it provides fairly decent protection on its "
"own."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool arming gloves"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"Tough cloth gloves made of layered wool quilting, thin enough to wear under "
"metal gauntlets.  They help to keep your hands safe during a fight."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "wool arming pants"
#: data/json/items/armor/gambesons.json
msgid ""
"Tough cloth pants worn alongside an aketon underneath metal armor.  This one"
" is made of layered wool quilting and it provides fairly decent protection "
"on its own."
msgstr ""

