#. ~ Description of "makeshift shotshell 'press'"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid ""
"A collection of items improvised for field reloading of shotshells.  A plank"
" with a hole cut in the center, a medium-sized nail, and a whittled dowel "
"are used to seat wads, decap primers, and (carefully!) reprime hulls.  "
"Powder and shot are measured with a cut-down shotshell hull.  The opposite "
"side of the plank has been shaped to allow for roll-crimping of the plastic "
"hulls.  There's no provision for resizing, so reloaded hulls will fire best "
"in the firearm they were fired from."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of "hand press"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
