#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
msgid "What got you out of the subway?"
msgstr "¿Y qué hizo que te fueras del subte?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/Backgrounds/evacuee_3.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"Woah, <name_g>, I don't even know where to start.  The riots?  I think it "
"was going on sooner than that.  There were bad murmurs going on a few weeks "
"before that happened.  Lots of really scary crimes, not your usual stuff but"
" like cannibalism and some real unspeakable shit, you know?  When the riots "
"started, I think I was already primed to think of it as something different "
"from a normal equality riot or anything like that.  I think that's part of "
"how I got out safer, I had had some time to get some stuff and get going, "
"and didn't try to make shopping trips.  People were abso-fuckin-lutely crazy"
" in those days.  It was a lot like the pandemic a few years back, except the"
" police were out in the streets in force, gunning people down like it was "
"going out of style."
msgstr ""
"Epa, <name_g>, no sé ni por donde empezar. ¿Los disturbios? Creo que empezó "
"antes de eso. Había un murmullo malo unas semanas antes de que pasar eso. "
"Muchos crímenes realmente siniestros, nada que ver con los normales, "
"canibalismo y mierdas muy difícil de explicar, ¿viste? Cuando comenzaron los"
" disturbios, creo que ya estaba convencido que era algo distinto a los "
"normales disturbios por la igualdad o cosas así. Creo que por eso pude salir"
" vivo, tuve tiempo de agarrar algunas cosas y salir, y no me detuve a "
"conseguir nada más. La gente estaba completamente loca por esos días. Se "
"parecía bastante a la pandemia de unos años antes, excepto que la calle "
"estaba llena de policía disparándole a la gente como si ya hubiera pasado de"
" moda."

