msgid ""
"Hey, did you notice that there's working wi-fi here?  Not that anything else"
" is online anymore, but still."
msgstr ""
"Hey, ¿te diste cuenta que acá hay wi-fi que funciona? Aunque no hay nada "
"online la verdad, pero igual."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Hey, did you notice that there's working wi-fi here?  Not that anything else"
" is online anymore, but still."
msgstr ""
"Hey, ¿te diste cuenta que acá hay wi-fi que funciona? Aunque no hay nada "
"online la verdad, pero igual."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hey, it can wait."
msgstr "Hey, puede esperar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hey, you have a map, don't you?  You can use mine, if you need."
msgstr "Hey, vos tenés un mapa, ¿no? Podés usar el mío, si necesitás."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Hmm?  Nothing, I guess I just like resting in this place.  I feel good "
"today."
msgstr ""
"¿Hmm? Nada, creo que me gusta descansar en este lugar. Me siento bien hoy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hold on, government documents?"
msgstr "Esperá un minuto, ¿documentos del gobierno?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Honestly, sometimes I feel like an ATM."
msgstr "Honestamente, a veces me siento como un cajero automático."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Hoo boy, yes they did, and let me tell you, they were not happy campers "
"about me crashing on their couch.  Now, these people don't tell me who they "
"are, but they tell me to get off the premises immediately.  I wasn't having "
"that.  I had been through hell and come out the other end, and I don't "
"remember what I said to them, but it was along the lines of 'I have nowhere "
"to go, and your building is nice and cozy, so if you want me to leave, you "
"can come out here and make me.'\"  They laugh.  \"They weren't expecting me "
"to bite back.  So I turn off the intercom and I go eat lunch.  When I go "
"back again, the first thing they ask is if I want a job."
msgstr ""
"Uh, sí, me contestaron, y te digo, no les gustaba nada que acampen en su "
"sillón. Ahora, esta gente no me dice quién es pero me dicen que me vaya del "
"predio inmediatamente. No me gustaba esa idea. Pasé por un infierno y ni me "
"acuerdo qué les dije pero era algo así como 'No tengo ningún lugar para ir y"
" este edificio es lindo y cómodo, así que si quieren que me vaya pueden "
"venir y hacerme ir.'\" Se rió. \"No esperaban que les respondiera así. Así "
"que apagué el intercomunicador y almorcé. Cuando lo volví a prender, lo "
"primero que me preguntaron era si estaba buscando trabajo."

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Appears in the the surface of Hub 01 as an external mercenary.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Hub Mercenary"
msgstr "Mercenario de Hub"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I appreciate it.  Here's the scrip; don't spend it all in one place."
msgstr ""
"Te lo agradezco. Acá tenés el pagaré, no te lo gastés todo en un lugar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I bought fruit and veggies from the store for my greens, but I figured those"
" didn't really have enough calories for the long-term, so I hunted.  To be "
"more accurate, I poached in the park I worked at.  It was never anything "
"huge; I had to be able to conceal this stuff, remember.  But we were on a "
"shoestring budget as it is and we never had the people we needed, so it was "
"trivial to bag an animal using a rifle from one of the ranger stations.  I'd"
" dress the carcass, then leave it in a place that I could either bring with "
"me in my truck that day or come back later to sneak it out.  I never got "
"caught.  I'm not proud of it, but I'm not really ashamed of it, either.  "
"Besides, venison is great."
msgstr ""
"Traje frutas y vegetales del almacén para tener verduras pero me di cuenta "
"que eso no tenía calorías suficientes para el largo plazo, así que salí a "
"cazar. Para ser más preciso, cazaba en el parque donde trabajaba. Nunca fue "
"algo grande, tenía que poder esconder esas cosas, acordate. Pero estábamos "
"complicados de presupuesto y nunca teníamos la gente que necesitábamos, así "
"que era común cazar un animal usando un rifle desde una de las estaciones de"
" guardabosques. Preparaba el cuerpo, luego lo dejaba en un lugar desde donde"
" podía traerlo en mi camioneta ese mismo día o volver después y sacarlo a "
"escondidas. Nunca me atraparon. No me siento orgulloso de eso pero tampoco "
"me da vergüenza. Además, la carne de ciervo está muy buena."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't have 200 gold for you right now."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't know what I was expecting."
msgstr "No sé qué estaba esperando."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I don't remember the video."
msgstr "No me acuerdo de ese video que decís."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I guess I am, yeah.  Feels like a stupid chore.\"  They suddenly pause.  "
"\"Hey.  If you happen across any gold out in the world, I'll pay you to "
"bring it back for me.  Right now my assignment stipulates eight scrip per "
"kilo, and I'd be willing to give you all of that.  I just want something "
"else to do.  Just maybe don't mention it to the intercom, alright?  This is "
"supposed to be my job."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I guess I am, yeah.  It feels nice to be putting all my skills to use instead of working an underpaid job to walk around the same woods flying a quadcopter around and being a glorified PR rep to cranky parents who are only at the park because they promised their kids they'd go.  Mind you, I'd still go back to it if I could.\"  Their expression falters a little.  \"We all had our struggles, but things are different now, you know?  We get to worry about the future in a whole new way; an existential way that we never had to consider before, not really.  Sure, there was the occasional nuke scare, but as a society, we had things pretty good.  Unless the dead stop getting back up, I… don't think things are going to ever go back to normal.\"\n"
"\n"
"Cranberry pauses for a moment, then shakes it off.  \"But… right now, I'm feeling at peace with everything, despite it all.  Maybe I'm just in shock, and it'll all come crashing down one of these days.  Things might get worse, and they may never get better.  But I feel alright.  And I think that's enough for me."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que estoy bien, sí. Se siente bien poder usar todas mis habilidades en lugar de trabajar por poca plata caminando por el mismo bosque, volando un cuadrirrotor y siendo un representante de relaciones públicas para unos padres mala onda que van al parque solamente porque se lo prometieron a sus hijos. Eso sí, volvería si pudiera.\" Su expresión titubea por un momento. \"Todos tenemos nuestros problemas pero las cosas son diferentes ahora, ¿viste? Tenemos que preocuparnos por el futuro de una forma completamente nueva; una manera existencial que nunca habíamos tenido que considerar, no realmente. Seguro, a veces estaba ese temor nuclear pero como sociedad teníamos las cosas bastante bien. Salvo que los muertos dejen de levantarse… no creo que las cosas vuelvan a la normalidad.\"\n"
"\n"
"Cranberry se queda callado por un instante, luego se sacudo. \"… en este momento, siento paz con todo, a pesar de las cosas. Tal vez esté en shock y me caiga todo junto uno de estos días. Las cosas se pueden poner peor y tal vez nunca vuelvan a estar bien. Pero me siento bien. Y creo que es suficiente para mí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I guess I could stay for a while."
msgstr "Supongo que me puedo quedar un rato."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I guess so.\"  They beam sheepishly.  \"Uh, call me Cranberry.  Cran is fine"
" too.  It's nice to meet someone else from here.  I guess having some "
"company for once wouldn't be awful."
msgstr ""
"Supongo.\" Sonríe tímidamente. \"Uh, decime Cranberry. O también Cran está "
"bien. Qué bueno conocer a alguien de otra parte. Supongo que tener un poco "
"de compañía no es un espanto."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I just realized, we've been in touch for a while now and I don't actually "
"know; are you a man or a woman?"
msgstr ""
"Me acabo de dar cuenta que ya estuvimos bastante tiempo en contacto y "
"todavía no sé; ¿sos hombre o mujer?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I kind of lost track of the days.  Every day was the same; eat, check the "
"barricades, look on the Internet, play some games with the sound off to try "
"and distract myself.  I filled up my bathtub, and once the water went out, "
"I'd drink from there when I needed to hydrate.  Meal planning got easier "
"after I was down to just my canned stuff.  The Internet didn't stay on for "
"long, though, which I guess was a blessing because of how many people were "
"sharing their fear and awful experiences in real time.  I did that routine "
"every day until that emergency broadcast came through that no help was "
"coming, and then I knew it was over."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I might not have the time.  Hold that thought for later."
msgstr "Me parece que no tengo tiempo. Quedate pensando en eso para después."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I sure did.  Sorry, just a stupid icebreaker.  Old habits and all that.\"  "
"They sit up.  \"What's up?"
msgstr ""
"Seguro. Perdón, era para romper el hielo. Una costumbre vieja, esas cosas.\""
" Se sienta. \"¿Cómo va?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I thought I was the only one working for the people here."
msgstr "Pensé que era el único que trabajaba para la gente de acá."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, that's a bit personal.  Like, you seem alright, but that's kind "
"of heavy stuff, y'know?  Maybe I can tell you another time."
msgstr ""
"Perdón pero eso es bastante personal. Mirá, me caés bien pero esas son cosas"
" pesadas, ¿entendés? Tal vez te lo pueda contar en otro momento."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sorry.  Too personal?"
msgstr "Perdoname. ¿Demasiado personal?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure we'll figure it out once there.  Bring a good weapon and some ammo "
"just in case, if you can; no idea what insanity <the_cataclysm> has brought "
"us this time."
msgstr ""
"Seguro que lo vamos a poder resolver cuando estemos ahí. Traé una buena arma"
" y un poco de munición por las dudas, si podés; no tengo idea qué locura nos"
" trajo el <the_cataclysm> esta vez."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "I'm sure."
msgstr "Estoy seguro."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"I've never really been a prepper, but I was into conspiracy theories.  Not "
"as a participant, just as an observer.  I think information spread is "
"interesting.\"  They pause.  \"I think it was in early March that I started "
"thinking something was wrong.  Like, the riots were bad beforehand, right?  "
"And that just seemed like normal unrest.  But then suddenly you're seeing it"
" happening in other countries where the normal explanations don't work.  So "
"I dug deeper, and once I did, I realized that this had been happening since "
"January, and getting worse since then.  That was when I started to take it "
"seriously."
msgstr ""
"Nunca fui un verdadero survivalista pero estaba pendiente de las teorías "
"conspirativas. No como participante, solamente como observador. Creo que la "
"difusión de la información es interesante.\" Para. \"Creo que fue en marzo "
"que empecé a pensar que algo andaba mal. Como que los disturbios estaban mal"
" antes, ¿no? Y eso parece como un malestar normal. Pero de repente, estás "
"viendo que pasa en otros países donde las explicaciones normales no "
"funcionaban. Así que profundicé y cuando lo hice, me di cuenta que estaba "
"pasando desde enero y se fue poniendo cada vez peor. Ahí fue cuando me lo "
"empecé a tomar en serio."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"If only, huh?  No, not quite.  About five miles away I hit a bad pothole and"
" skidded off the road and got stuck.  That's not a problem on its own, but a"
" few minutes into trying to get it unstuck, I saw a big furrow of dirt "
"coming towards me and decided, you know what, maybe I should get off the "
"side of the road.  So I grab my bugout bag from the cabin and a little food "
"from the bed, and I book it onto the road.  Now, I don't know what this "
"thing was, but it hit the truck from below and *flipped it over*.  That was "
"enough to make me say 'Nope, I can go on foot.'"
msgstr ""
"Si hubiera sido así, ¿no? Pero no, no exactamente. Unos diez kilómetros "
"después me comí un bache y derrapé hasta quedar encajado al costado de la "
"ruta. Eso no es un problema por sí mismo pero después de estar unos minutos "
"tratando de desencajarla, vi una montaña de tierra que venía hacia mí y "
"decidí que tal vez debería correrme, ¿viste?. Así que agarré el bolso de la "
"cabina y un poco de comida de la caja y me fui corriendo por la ruta. Ahora,"
" no sé qué era eso pero golpeó la camioneta desde abajo y la dió vuelta. Y "
"fue suficiente para hacerme decir 'No, no puedo andar a pie.'"

#. ~ Description of mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Investigate Hub 01's radio tower, discover the source of the interference, "
"and fix the problem."
msgstr ""
"Investigá la torre de radio del Hub 01, descrbrí la fuente de la "
"interferencia y arreglá el problema."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"It took a bit for me to muster the nerve to leave, but I wanted to.  Had to "
"see, y'know?  It was… a shock, zombies just walking in the parking lot.  "
"Like, sure, I could look out the window, but it feels different up close.  I"
" had my knife handy, and I didn't want to make too much noise, so that's "
"what I used.  I stabbed one of my dead neighbors in the neck that day.\"  "
"They smile wistfully.  \"I threw up on my shoes after the first one, but it "
"got easier."
msgstr ""
"Me costó un poco armarme de coraje para irme pero quería irme. Tenía que "
"verlo, ¿entendés? Fue un… shock, zombis caminando en la playa de "
"estacionamiento. O sea, sí, podía mirar por la ventana pero se siente "
"distinto de cerca. Tenía mi cuchillo a mano y no quería hacer mucho ruido, "
"así que usé eso. Apuñalé a uno de mis vecinos muertos en el cuello ese "
"día.\" Sonreía tristemente. \"Me vomité las zapatillas después del primero "
"pero se fue poniendo más fácil."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"It took me a few days from there.  I had a heavy load, and it was slow "
"going.  I slept on the road the first night because I was so freaked out by "
"what I saw, but the day after I got the nerves to walk through the woods.  I"
" had a tent, so it wasn't so bad.  Every now and then, I'd run into a "
"zombie, or a wrecked car that still had some of them buckled in.  I left my "
"shotgun behind in the truck, so I got better at using the knife.  It gets "
"easier, y'know?"
msgstr ""
"Tardé unos días desde ahí. Iba bastante cargado y el camino era lento. Dormí"
" en la ruta la primera noche porque estaba muy asustado por lo que vi, pero "
"al día siguiente tuve el coraje suficiente para caminar por el bosque. Tenía"
" una carpa así que no estaba tan mal. De vez en cuando, me cruzaba con un "
"zombi o con un auto destruido que todavía tenía alguno enganchado con el "
"cinturón de seguridad. Dejé mi escopeta en la camioneta así que me volví "
"mejor usando el cuchillo. Se va haciendo cada vez más sencillo, ¿viste?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just like that?"
msgstr "¿Así nomás?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just saying hi.  I'll be on my way now."
msgstr "Saludando, nomás. Ya me voy yendo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Just the same as you.  Some nobody doing dirty work for scraps.  Uh, no "
"offense."
msgstr ""
"Lo mismo que vos. Un don nadie haciendo trabajos sucios a cambio chatarra. "
"Uh, sin ofender."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Just trying to get some rest.  I don't have anywhere else to stay, so they "
"let me sleep on the couch out here as long as I keep my gun handy."
msgstr ""
"Intentando descansar un poco. No tengo otro lugar donde quedarme así que me "
"dejan dormir en el sillón acá afuera siempre que tenga mi arma cerca."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just vibing."
msgstr "Relajándome."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Just wondering if things will get better someday."
msgstr "Me pregunto si alguna vez mejorarán las cosas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Let's get back home."
msgstr "Volvamos a casa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Let's set up a combat strategy."
msgstr "Vamos a establecer la estrategia de combate."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"March 30th happened.\"  Cranberry seems shaken, and talks a little louder "
"for a second.  \"You remember that video, right?  That was what set off "
"alarm bells in my head.  That shit was fucking scary.  And at that point I "
"realized, okay, I think things are about to get bad and this is for real."
msgstr ""
"Pasó lo del 30 de marzo.\" Cranberry parece perturbado y habla un poco más "
"fuerte por un instante. \"Te acordás de ese video, ¿no? Eso fue lo que me "
"hizo prender las alarmas. Eso me hizo cagar todo. En ese momento me dije, "
"okay, creo que las cosas están por ponerse mal y esto va en serio."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"My truck was still there, and was on half a tank of gas.  I thought, okay, "
"this isn't gonna be easy, but I can pack my food and the things I need to "
"take with me into the truck, and then drive to that building I know about "
"that was so reinforced.\"  They gesture around them.  \"This building.  The "
"Hub.  So I got some stuff into a bugout bag in the cabin and filled up the "
"truck bed, and off I went.  The roads were bad, but I'm not a bad driver.  "
"Zombies are slow."
msgstr ""
"Mi camioneta todavía estaba ahí y tenía medio tanque lleno. Pensé, bueno, no"
" va a ser fácil pero puedo agarrar mi comida y las cosas que necesito y "
"manejar hasta ese edificio que sabía que estaba bien reforzado.\" Señaló a "
"su alrededor. \"Este edificio. El Hub. Así que junté algunas cosas en un "
"bolso en la cabina y llené la caja de la camioneta y me fui. Las rutas "
"estaban complicadas pero manejo bastante bien. Los zombis son lentos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"No, no!  It's fine, promise.  It's just been a hot minute, and I'm trying to"
" remember it.  It's been a while.  You sure you want to hear it?"
msgstr ""
"¡No, no! Está bien, te juro. Fue hace un rato y estoy intentando recordarlo."
" Pasó mucho tiempo. ¿Seguro que querés escucharlo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "None taken.  I guess that makes two of us."
msgstr "No me ofendo. Supongo que somos dos, entonces."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Not a whole lot, really.  They made me track down and destroy some "
"government documents a while back.  Obviously I read them first, but it "
"wasn't much.  As far as I know, this place had an experimental computer "
"network before everything went to hell.  What's going on in there now is "
"anybody's guess."
msgstr ""
"La verdad que no mucho. Me hicieron rastrear y destruir unos documentos del "
"gobierno hace un tiempo. Obviamente que los leí primero pero no eran gran "
"cosa. Hasta donde yo sé, este lugar tenía una red experimental de "
"computadoras antes de que todo se vaya al carajo. Pero nadie sabe qué está "
"pasando acá ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Now that you mention it, it does seem rather strange."
msgstr "Ahora que lo decís, la verdad que parece raro."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"People started freaking out.  I did, too.  I don't know how bad things got elsewhere, but shit was flying off the shelves where I lived.  Empty racks at grocery stores everywhere you looked.  I had enough food for a few weeks, so it wasn't a problem for me, but it still shook me up bad.  Every day some horrible new shit was happening somewhere in the world, and things got just worse and worse.  Then that insanity with Rhode Island happened, and once the national emergency came out, I knew that okay, this is happening, it's actually happening.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"Did you know that I was still going to work that entire time?  I don't know, it just felt meditative.  I lived in a pretty rural area, so there wasn't the kind of chaos in the cities and congestion on the roads.  I could just take a side road there and have a day of quiet.  Just the woods and whoever else actually bothered to show up that day.  The park closed for visitors closed a day or two before the state of emergency, and it was really peaceful, being there alone."
msgstr ""
"La gente empezó a volverse loca. Yo también. No sabía cómo estaban las cosas en otros lugares pero donde yo vivía ya se había ido todo a la mierda. Ya no quedaba nada en las góndolas de los supermercados. Yo tenía comida para unas semanas así que ese no era un problema, pero igual me dejó shokeado. Todos los días pasaba alguna mierda nueva en alguna parte del mundo y las cosas fueron empeorando. Después pasó esa locura en Rhode Island y cuando se declaró la emergencia nacional, entendí que era todo muy real, que estaba sucediendo realmente.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"¿Sabías que todavía iba a trabajar durante todo ese momento? No sé, me sentía meditativo. Vivía en un área bastante rural, así que no había el mismo caos que en las ciudades y la congestión en las rutas. Me podía ir por una ruta secundaria y tener un día de tranquilidad. El bosque y alguno que otro que decidía molestarme ese día. El parque estaba cerrado para los visitantes desde uno o dos días antes del estado de emergencia, y era un lugar verdaderamente tranquilo, podía estar solo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Return to Hub 01"
msgstr "Regresar al Hub 01"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
msgid "Rough out there, isn't it?"
msgstr "Está complicado ahí afuera, ¿no?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"So I figured that this wasn't going to be a problem a few months down the "
"line, right?  Just a flash in the pan.  I had my emergency stock of food in "
"case things went bad for a little while.  Best case scenario, I never have "
"to worry about it, things go back to normal after a bit, and I save some "
"money on groceries for a while.  And I wanted to keep doing this for a few "
"more weeks, but…"
msgstr ""
"Así que me di cuenta que esto no iba a ser un problema por unos meses, "
"¿viste? Pura espuma. Tenía mi suministro de comida de emergencia por si las "
"cosas andaban mal por un tiempo. En el mejor de los casos, nunca me tendría "
"que preocupar por eso, las cosas volverían a la normalidad en un tiempo y me"
" ahorraría plata en comida. Y quería seguir haciéndolo por unas semanas más "
"pero…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "So what's going on?"
msgstr "¿Qué anda pasando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Strange bedfellows…"
msgstr "Extraños compañeros…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Sure seems like it.  What even was that…?  Eh, doesn't matter.  Let's go "
"back to the Hub; hopefully the tower's working now."
msgstr ""
"Parecería que sí. ¿Qué era eso…? Eh, no importa. Volvamos al Hub, con suerte"
" la torre ahora está funcionando."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Surprise!\"  They do jazz hands.  \"Sorry.  Well, I'm told that I'm part of "
"a small group right now.  Maybe you were the first."
msgstr ""
"¡Sorpresa!\" Hace manitos de jazz. \"Perdón. Bueno, me dijeron que soy parte"
" de un pequeño grupo ahora. Tal vez vos fuiste el primero."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Surprise!\"  They do jazz hands.  \"Sorry.  Well, I'm told that I'm part of "
"a small group right now.  Maybe you were the first."
msgstr ""
"¡Sorpresa!\" Hace manitos de jazz. \"Perdón. Bueno, me dijeron que soy parte"
" de un pequeño grupo ahora. Tal vez vos fuiste el primero."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Surprise!\"  They do jazz hands.  \"Sorry.  Well, I'm told that I'm part of "
"a small group right now.  Maybe you were the first."
msgstr ""
"¡Sorpresa!\" Hace manitos de jazz. \"Perdón. Bueno, me dijeron que soy parte"
" de un pequeño grupo ahora. Tal vez vos fuiste el primero."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thank you for telling me."
msgstr "Gracias por contarme."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot for having my back.  Like I said, I owe you one."
msgstr "Muchas gracias por cuidarme la espalda. Como dije, te debo una."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thanks a lot."
msgstr "Muchas gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Thanks.  I never thought I'd get exhausted of carrying pure gold around, but"
" here we are."
msgstr ""
"Gracias. Nunca pensé que me iba a cansar de llevar oro puro pero así "
"estamos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"That's quite the story.  You seem to be feeling pretty good, in spite of the"
" world ending."
msgstr ""
"Qué buena historia. Parece que estás bastante bien, a pesar del fin del "
"mundo y todo eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"That's what the news said, anyway.  It was only about a 20-minute trip from "
"my apartment and sometimes I'd drive past it, so I was curious and I did "
"some research into it.  The only info I could find about it online said that"
" it was a NASA lab for computer research, but that was probably bullshit.  I"
" mean, do you see any NASA logos?  Sure, we got huge steel doors and 15-foot"
" concrete walls, but not a logo in sight.  The building probably goes "
"underground, right?  It's way too small to be a whole laboratory up here."
msgstr ""
"Pero eso era lo que decían las noticias. Fue solo un viaje de unos 20 "
"minutos hasta mi departamento y a veces pasaba por ahí, así que me agarró "
"curiosidad e hice algunas investigaciones. La única información que pude "
"encontrar online decía que era una laboratorio de la NASA para investigación"
" informática, pero probablemente era mentira. Quiero decir, ¿viste algún "
"logo de la NASA? Seguro, tiene puertas enormes de acero y paredes de "
"concreto de cuatro metros y medio pero ni un solo logo. Probablemente, el "
"edificio continúe abajo de la tierra, ¿no? Es demasiado chico para ser un "
"laboratorio entero arriba."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Then the portals happened, and you know the rest from there.  Two days "
"later, the world was over.  There was a lot of chaos in my complex.  I just "
"nailed shut my front door, drew all the curtains, kept my shotgun loaded, "
"and probably slept maybe ten hours total that week.  I don't know if there "
"was someone up in the sky watching over me, but if there was, I sure as hell"
" owe them big time."
msgstr ""
"Y después empezaron los portales y ya sabés cómo fue el resto. Dos días "
"después, el mundo se terminó. Hubo mucho caos en mi complejo. Cerré con "
"clavos la puerta de adelante, cerré todas las cortinas, mantuve mi escopeta "
"cargada y esa semana debo haber dormido diez horas en total, probablemente. "
"No sé si había alguien en el cielo cuidándome pero si había, le debo mucho."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "They don't let you in to sleep?"
msgstr "¿No te dejan dormir adentro?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Thinking I should go hunt something soon…"
msgstr "Estoy pensando que voy a tener que ir a cazar algo pronto…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Uh… okay.  Who are you?"
msgstr "Ah… okay. ¿Quién sos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something else?"
msgstr "¿Querés que te ayude con algo más?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Want help with something?"
msgstr "¿Querés ayudarme con algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, I should get going."
msgstr "Bueno, me tengo que ir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, never mind."
msgstr "Bueno, no importa."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Well, no.  It was obvious they just wanted to get rid of me, but I decided I wanted to show that I was useful.  They tell me to find a crashed drone somewhere in the surrounding area and bring it back here.  No directions, of course.  Y'know, go find this drone in the middle of the woods, it'll be easy.  But I had some tools in my bag, right?  And yours truly has repaired some drones in the park service.\"\n"
"\n"
"\"So it takes me a whole-ass afternoon, but I find their stupid drone stuck in a tree.  I can see the camera's still on, so I pick it up and I tell the lens: 'Hey, you want me to fix it too?'  And I do.  It was just a cracked frame and the wiring to the rotors was sliced up.  The propellers themselves were fine.  So I bring it out of the woods and turn it off.  Then I open up the casing, solder up the wires, and use superglue to hold the frame together, which wasn't perfect, but I figured it'd hold until it got back home.  Then I turned it back on, and wouldn't you know, it immediately starts up and sits there for a minute, like 'What the fuck?  Why am I working again?'  And then it flies away, and I walk my smug ass back home."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Well, thanks for offering."
msgstr "Bueno, gracias por el ofrecimiento."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Active Noise Control"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Well… a little while ago, I set up a radio transmitter in the radio tower "
"not far from here, but apparently it's stopped transmitting.  If you're "
"willing to back me up while I check it out, I'll owe you a favor."
msgstr ""
"Bueno… hace un tiempo establecí un transmisor de radio en la torre que está "
"acá cerca pero aparentemente dejó de transmitir. Si tenés ganas de ir a "
"revisarlo, te voy a deber un favor."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What do you know about our employers?"
msgstr "¿Qué sabés sobre nuestros jefes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What food were you canning?"
msgstr "¿Y qué comida enlatabas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "What was <the_cataclysm> like for you?"
msgstr "¿Cómo anda el <the_cataclysm> para vos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
#: data/json/npcs/other/TALK_ANIMAL_SHELTER_SURVIVOR.json
msgid "Who are you, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Quién sos vos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid "Who exactly are you?"
msgstr "¿Quién sos exactamente?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Whoo-ee, someone was living under a rock, huh?  It was all over the news.  "
"Video on YouTube, it was a livestream of one of the riots in Minneapolis.  A"
" mom was…\"  They hesitate.  \"I don't want to go into detail, but it was "
"real bad.  Real bad.  That's what set off people panicking."
msgstr ""
"Bue, alguien vivía adentro de un taper, eh. Estaba en todos los noticieros. "
"Un video de YouTube, era una transmisión en vivo de uno de los disturbios en"
" Minéapolis. Una madre estaba…\" Duda. \"No quiero entrar en detalles pero "
"era muy malo. Muy malo. Eso fue lo que hizo que la gente entrara en pánico."

#. ~ Description of mission "Return to Hub 01"
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"With the source of the radio tower's interference fixed, return to Hub 01 "
"with Cranberry."
msgstr ""
"Con la fuente de interferencia de la torre de radio arreglada, volver al Hub"
" 01 con Cranberry."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Wondering if the whole world is like this now.  It has to be, right?  I was "
"watching some foreign news channels when everything was going down, and it "
"sounded like things were just as bad there…"
msgstr ""
"Me preguntaba si el mundo entero está así ahora. Debería, ¿no? Estaba viendo"
" noticias de canales extranjeros cuando todo se fue a la mierda y parecía "
"que las cosas estaban tan mal como acá…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgid ""
"Yeah!  Crazy shit.  They sent me to an office building to find a folder with"
" a certain serial and get rid of it.  They didn't even care what was on it."
"  By the time I got there, though, the building was pretty much a wreck.  "
"The folder had been sitting in a puddle for God knows how long, and there "
"was nothing even remotely legible by then."
msgstr ""
"¡Sí! Una locura. Me mandaron a un edificio de oficinas para encontrar una "
"carpeta con un número específico y deshacerme de ella. Ni siquiera les "
"importaba qué contenía. Pero para cuando llegué, el edificio estaba en "
"ruinas. La carpeta estaba tirada en un charco, andá a saber cuánto tiempo "
"estuvo ahí, y ya no tenía nada ni remotamente legible."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/hub01/NPC_Cranberry_Foster.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Yeah.  Have you noticed how they pay us in these tiny little gold coins?\"  "
"Cranberry holds one up for emphasis.  \"It's bizarre.  You'd think they have"
" a gold mine in there, but no, they don't, so they make me cross the damn "
"world grabbing gold bars.  As far as scrip goes, it seems inconvenient as "
"hell to make."
msgstr ""
"Sí. ¿Te diste cuenta que nos pagan en estas pequeñas monedas doradas?\" "
"Cranberry sostiene una para darle énfasis. \"Es una locura. Pensarías que "
"tienen una mina de oro acá pero no, no tienen así que me hacen cruzar todo "
"el mundo buscando lingotes de oro. Y según la receta, hacerlas es más "
"inconveniente que la mierda."

