#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Hold the horses, pal.  Nobody allowed you to stay here - yet."
msgstr "Pará la moto, amigo. Nadie te permitió quedarte acá - todavía."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Huh, even so?  I'm not saying I approve your… tastes, but I definitely "
"respect people who use all possibilities life has to offer."
msgstr ""
"¿Huh, sí? No digo que apruebe tus… gustos, pero definitivamente respeto a la"
" gente que utiliza todas las posibilidades que la vida ofrece."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get the military ID card from the chief's
#. office"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "Huh.  This isn't going to work like I thought."
msgstr "Ah. Esto no va a funcionar como lo pensé."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I don't know if I'll take your advice, but thanks nevertheless."
msgstr "No sé si voy a seguir tu consejo pero gracias igual."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I guess I need to find some other place…"
msgstr "Supongo que voy a tener que buscar otro lugar…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I have a bad feeling about this.  Sorry, I'll pass."
msgstr "Tengo un mal presentimiento con esto. Perdón pero paso."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I just wanted to ask if you have a job for me."
msgstr "Quería preguntarte si tenés un trabajo para mí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I killed tons of <zombies> while I was trying to get this thing.  Do you "
"really think you and your handful of losers pose a threat to me?"
msgstr ""
"Maté bochas de <zombies> para conseguir esta cosa. ¿En serio te pensás que "
"vos y tu puñado de idiotas es una amenaza para mí?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get the military ID card from the chief's
#. office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I need the military ID card from the chief's safe in his office.  I don't "
"mean the warden, I mean the chief corrections officer, you hear me?  Just "
"bring that thing to me and I'll help you.  Deal?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I need you to retrieve some stuff from a locked safe.  Interested?"
msgstr "Necesito conseguir unas cosas de una caja fuerte. ¿Estás interesado?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I want to get out of this <swear> prison.  I hoped you could help me with "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Me quiero ir de esta cárcel de <swear>. Esperaba que vos me pudieras ayudar "
"a eso."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I went through incredible hardships to get it.  Please, can I keep this to "
"myself?"
msgstr ""
"Pasé por adversidades increíbles para conseguirlo. Por favor, ¿podría "
"quedármelo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I'm afraid you're not in the position to demand anything from me, <name_b>."
"  <get_lost>"
msgstr ""
"Lamentablemente, no estás en posición de demandarme nada, <name_b>. "
"<get_lost>"

#. ~ Job description of "Prisoner" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I'm here to kick ass."
msgstr "Vine a romper culos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"I'm just hungry, and I thought you might give me some food for some job."
msgstr ""
"Tengo hambre y pensé que podías darme comida a cambio de ayudarte con algo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "I'm on my way."
msgstr "Estoy yendo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"It was a nightmare, lots of <zombies>, blood everywhere!  Thank god I'm "
"among living people again."
msgstr ""
"Fue una pesadilla, muchos <zombies>, ¡sangre por todas partes! Gracias a "
"dios puedo contarme entre los vivos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "It would be you who will regret talking to me like that."
msgstr "Vos vas a ser el que te arrepientas de hablarme así."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Let's say that's none of your <swear> business.  Other questions?"
msgstr ""
"Digamos que eso no es de tu importancia de <swear>. ¿Alguna otra pregunta?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Nice talking to ya.  Farewell."
msgstr "Fue bueno hablar con vos. Hasta luego."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "No, of course not!  Sorry, I'm leaving."
msgstr "¡No, claro que no! Perdón, ya me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Not so fast, I think you need to pay for breaking your promise and bothering"
" me.  Give me your shit, now!"
msgstr ""
"No tan rápido, creo que necesitás pagar por romper tu promesa y molestarme. "
"¡Dame tus cosas, ahora!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Noted.  Bye."
msgstr "Lo anota. Chau."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, I'm listening."
msgstr "Ok, te escucho."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, sorry, I promise I won't bother you anymore."
msgstr "Ok, perdón, prometo no volver a molestarte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Ok, sorry, I'm already leaving!"
msgstr "Ok, perdón, ¡ya me estoy yendo!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Okay, fine.  Cheapskate!"
msgstr "Ok, bueno. ¡Amarrete!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Okay.  It was convincing.  I'll still get what I want, one way or another.  "
"You better watch your back from now on."
msgstr ""
"Bueno. Fue convincente. Igual me quedo con lo que quería, de una manera u "
"otra. Empezá a cuidarte la espalda de ahora en más."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Please don't hurt me!  Take all that you want."
msgstr "¡Por favor, no me hagas nada! Llevate lo que quieras."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Please!  I don't want to go back there!  I'm tired and hungry!  I just need "
"time to rest!"
msgstr ""
"¡Por favor! ¡No quiero volver ahí! ¡Estoy cansado y con hambre! ¡Necesito un"
" poco de descanso!"

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ Skills intentionally kept low.  This character should probably have a
#. higher chance of having insanity type traits eventually.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/npcs/prisoners/mi-go_prisoners.json
msgid "Prisoner"
msgstr "Preso"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Shit!  Looks like I'm on my own now.  Thanks for nothing.  Bye."
msgstr "¡Mierda! Parece que estoy solo ahora. Gracias por nada. Chau."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "That's weird."
msgstr "Es medio raro."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"The answer is still no.  In fact it might be better for us to kill you right"
" away - you know, the less mouths to feed, the better.  But I'm in a good "
"mood today, so I've decided to help you get out of this island."
msgstr ""
"La respuesta sigue siendo que no. De hecho, sería mejor que te matemos ahora"
" - mirá, menos bocas para alimentar, mejor. Pero estoy de buen humor hoy, "
"así que decidí ayudarte a salir de esta isla."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get the military ID card from the chief's
#. office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"The chief's office is on the other side of the prison.  I think the road "
"there is full of <zombies>, so you better find a weapon.  Also you probably "
"will need some tools to crack the safe open."
msgstr ""
"La oficina del jefe está en el otro lado de la cárcel. Creo que el camino "
"hasta ahí está lleno de <zombies>, así que te conviene llevar un arma. "
"También vas a necesitar algunas herramientas para poder abrir la caja "
"fuerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Wait, what?  A <swear> can of beans?!  I went through hell to get this "
"<swear> thing for you, and all you give me as reward is a <swear> can of "
"beans?!  I demand something more substantial."
msgstr ""
"¿Esperá, qué? ¡¿Una <swear> lata de porotos?! Pasé por todo este infierno de"
" <swear> para vos y ¡¿todo lo que me das como recompensa es una lata de "
"porotos de <swear>?! Exijo algo más sustancial."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"We don't have much space, and there's not much food.  Besides, I don't know "
"you at all, and something tells me you won't survive another day."
msgstr ""
"No tenemos mucho lugar y no hay mucha comida. Además, no te conozco y algo "
"me dice que no podrías sobrevivir ni un día más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"Well, that's a boastful statement.  Not that I don't believe it, it's just…."
"  Ah, nevermind.  Let's get to the point.  What do you want?"
msgstr ""
"Bueno, esa es una afirmación presuntuosa. No es que no lo crea, solo que…. "
"Ah, no importa. Vamos al punto. ¿Qué querés?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What for do you need it?"
msgstr "¿Para que lo necesitás?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What's in the safe?"
msgstr "¿Qué hay en la caja fuerte?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "What, <no>!"
msgstr "¡Qué, <no>!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, I got it.  See ya."
msgstr "Sí, entiendo. Nos vemos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, I've been through situations far worse than that."
msgstr "Sí, ya pasé por situaciones mucho peores que esta."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Snippet in category "schizo_self_talk"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
#: data/json/snippets/schizophrenia.json
msgid "Yeah, sure."
msgstr "Sí, seguro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "Yeah, we share the same opinions on this matter."
msgstr "Sí, compartimos la misma opinión en este tema."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You know, I think I'll manage without your help.  Bye."
msgstr "Mirá, creo que voy a poder manejarme sin tu ayuda. Chau."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid "You think you're immortal, huh, <name_b>?"
msgstr "¿Te pensás que sos inmortal, eh, <name_b>?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid "You think you're immortal, huh, <name_b>?"
msgstr "¿Te pensás que sos inmortal, eh, <name_b>?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "You think you're immortal, huh, <name_b>?"
msgstr "¿Te pensás que sos inmortal, eh, <name_b>?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Get the military ID card from the chief's
#. office"
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "You're useless.  I should've killed you when I met you."
msgstr ""
"Sos un inútil. Te tendría que haber matado cuando te vi la primera vez."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid ""
"[CANNIBAL] It's hard to die of hunger when there's so many tasty corpses "
"lying around."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[Ecology 2] I have some survival expertise!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[STR 11] I'm tougher than it seems!"
msgstr "[FUE 11] ¡Me la banco mucho más de lo que parece!"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "[Show the military ID card.] You mean this stuff?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Former prisoner with a melee or ranged weapon and prison clothing.
#. Sometimes they also have prison guards' gear.
#: data/json/npcs/island_prison/prisoners.json
msgid "gatekeeper"
msgstr "carcelero"

