"I used to travel a lot before <the_cataclysm>, and I've had this camper with"
" me for a while now.  I was at home when the riots started, so I grabbed "
"everything I could from my house and hopped in the camper.  I nearly wrecked"
" on my way out of town when some crazy people tried to smash my van, but I "
"made it out.  I've been on the move ever since."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid ""
"I'll be gone here in a day or two, just stopping long enough to get some "
"supplies and fix anything wrong with the camper."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Let's take a look."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Sweet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that cabin"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that desolate barn"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Check out that collapsed house"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "That's unfortunate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid ""
"What's in that RV of yours?  Couldn't be anything you need, so hand over "
"your stuff."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "When will you be leaving?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where did you say you were going again?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where was the bunker at?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/camper_van_traveler.json
msgid "Where were they at?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"*tips their hat down from their eyes and looks at you blearily.  \"Huh?  "
"Hey, I'm tryin'a sleep here.  I was on night watch."
msgstr ""
"*inclina el sombrero y te mira con sueño. \"¿Eh? Hey, estoy tratando dormir."
" Estuve en el turno noche."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Actually I had a little more to trade still."
msgstr "En realidad, todavía tengo un poco más que me gustaría negociar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Always good to do a little trading."
msgstr "Siempre es bueno comerciar un poco."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Are you threatening me?"
msgstr "¿Me estás amenazando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Can you give me directions to any of these other survivor groups?"
msgstr ""
"¿Me podés dar indicaciones hacia alguno de esos otros grupos de "
"sobrevivientes?"

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, tells you about being a guard and directs you
#. to free merchants.
#. ~ Random NPC, non persistent, doesn't have much to say.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Caravan Guard"
msgstr "Guardia de Caravana"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  Feel free to come by and trade, or if "
"you're the type, we might have use for your services as a merc."
msgstr ""
"Acá, lo voy a marcar en tu mapa. Vení cuando quieras a comerciar o, si sos "
"de esa clase, podrías usar tus servicios como mercenario."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hey, thanks.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Hey, gracias. Bueno, vamos a ver qué podemos negociar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Hi again.  You want something?"
msgstr "Hola, otra vez. ¿Querías algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "How do I get there?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo llego hasta ahí?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I can understand that.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Entiendo. Bueno, veamos qué podemos negociar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "I won't try anything if you don't.  Just passing through."
msgstr ""
"No voy a hacer nada raro si vos no hacés nada raro. Solamente estoy pasando "
"por acá."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm a caravan guard, working for the Free Merchants.  I'm an independent "
"contractor though.  Seems like a good way to get safety in numbers and try "
"to find a safe place to settle down."
msgstr ""
"Soy guardia de la caravana, trabajo para los Mercaderes Libres. Pero soy "
"contratista independiente. Parece una buena manera de estar seguros siendo "
"muchos e intentar encontrar un lugar a salvo donde establecernos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"I'm good for the moment, but you can usually find a merc or two waiting "
"between jobs, back at the Free Merchant base."
msgstr ""
"Por ahora estoy bien pero generalmente, podés encontrar algún mercenario "
"esperando trabajo en la base de los Mercaderes Libres."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "It's a living, eh?  I'd better get going."
msgstr "Es una manera de vivir, eh. Mejor me voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers "
"directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr ""
"Sin ofender pero definitivamente mis clientes no querrían que le de su "
"ubicación a un extraño. Vas a tener que encontrarlos por tus propios medios."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers "
"directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr ""
"Sin ofender pero definitivamente mis clientes no querrían que le de su "
"ubicación a un extraño. Vas a tener que encontrarlos por tus propios medios."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"No offense, but my clients definitely would not like me giving strangers "
"directions to their hideouts.  You'll have to find them on their own terms."
msgstr ""
"Sin ofender pero definitivamente mis clientes no querrían que le de su "
"ubicación a un extraño. Vas a tener que encontrarlos por tus propios medios."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"No, not at all.  Just being cautious.  You know how it gets out here.  We're"
" not looking for trouble.  In fact, if you've got anything worthwhile, maybe"
" we could do a little trading."
msgstr ""
"No, para nada. Solamente estoy siendo precavido. Sabés cómo se pone acá, no "
"estamos buscando problemas. De hecho, si tenés algo de valor tal vez podamos"
" comerciar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nope, just saying hi."
msgstr "Nop, solamente pasaba a saludar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Nothing much.  Just passing through."
msgstr "No mucho. Solamente, pasando por acá."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, uh, sorry."
msgstr "Oh, uh, perdón."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "So you're working for these guys, but aren't one of them?"
msgstr "Así que estás trabajando para esta gente pero ¿no sos uno de ellos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Sup?  Nice to see a survivor.  If you're here for business, talk to the "
"trader."
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo va? Qué bueno ver otro sobreviviente. Si estás acá para hacer algún "
"negocio, hablá con el comerciante."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, I can mark it on your map if you like.  Here."
msgstr "Seguro, te lo puedo marcar en tu mapa si querés. Mirá."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Sure, let's trade."
msgstr "Seguro, a ver qué podemos negociar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for chatting.  I'd better go."
msgstr "Gracias por la charla. Mejor me voy yendo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for that.  I'd better go."
msgstr "Gracias por eso. Mejor me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "¡Gracias por el consejo! Voy a seguir mi camino."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip!  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "¡Gracias por el consejo! ¿Qué me estabas diciendo antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the tip."
msgstr "Gracias por el consejo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks.  What were we talking about before?"
msgstr "Gracias. ¿De qué estábamos hablando antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "That suits me fine.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "Eso me parece bien. Voy a seguir mi camino."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "That's interesting.  Well, let's trade."
msgstr "Interesante. Bueno, a ver qué podemos negociar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "That's it?  What's your story?"
msgstr "¿Eso es todo? ¿Cuál es su historia?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"The Free Merchants?  Do they have some kind of trade outpost or anything "
"like that?"
msgstr ""
"¿Los Mercaderes Libres? ¿Tienen alguna clase de puesto de comercio o algo "
"como eso?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're just travelers, making a pit stop.  Might be willing to trade a bit, "
"if you've got anything to share.  We're not looking for trouble, there's "
"plenty of that on the roads already."
msgstr ""
"Solo somos viajeros haciendo una parada técnica. Podría ser buena idea "
"comerciar, si tenés algo para compartir. No estamos buscando problemas, ya "
"hay muchos de esos por los caminos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're with a larger group of survivors, working out of one of the old FEMA "
"bunkers.  Folks have taken to calling us Free Merchants, although that "
"sounds kinda on the nose to me.  We know about a few survivor groups and we "
"make regular trips around, sharing supplies back and forth and bringing them"
" home.  We're on the way back now."
msgstr ""
"Estamos con un grupo más grande de sobrevivientes, trabajando en uno de los "
"viejos búnker de FEMA. Algunos nos llaman Mercaderes Libres, y eso me parece"
" que suena bastante exacto. Sabemos que existen algunos grupos de "
"sobrevivientes y hacemos viajes regularmente por acá, compartiendo nuestras "
"cosas y llevando y trayendo hacia nuestra casa. Ahora estamos volviendo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here "
"and we're well armed."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, bueno, otro viajero. No intentes nada raro, somos muchos más y "
"estamos armados"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:m"
msgid ""
"Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here "
"and we're well armed."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, bueno, otro viajero. No intentes nada raro, somos muchos más y "
"estamos armados"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgctxt "u:n"
msgid ""
"Well well, another traveler.  Don't try anything, you're outnumbered here "
"and we're well armed."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, bueno, otro viajero. No intentes nada raro, somos muchos más y "
"estamos armados"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "What's your deal here?"
msgstr "¿Qué es esto?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "Where is 'home'?"
msgstr "¿Y dónde está su 'casa'?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, these guys snagged some kind of FEMA evacuation bunker during the "
"early part of <the_cataclysm> and hoard the space.  They don't let anyone "
"else join, but they need supplies, so they send out traders, and those "
"traders need protection, so they send out guys like me."
msgstr ""
"Sí, estos tipos agarraron una especie de búnker de FEMA durante la primera "
"parte del <the_cataclysm> y acapararon el lugar. No dejan que nadie más se "
"les una pero necesitan suministros así que mandan comerciantes, y esos "
"comerciantes necesitan protección así que los mandan con tipos como yo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/free_merchant_caravans.json
msgid "You looking for work?  I might be hiring."
msgstr "¿Estás buscando trabajo? Estoy buscando gente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"If you can call it that, sure.  So maybe we should do our best"
" to be better at that than the zombies.  Seems pretty reasonable to me, and "
"it's a pretty low bar to clear.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe. \"Podés decirle así si querés, sí. Así que tal vez tengamos que "
"hacer mejor trabajo que los zombis en eso. A mí me parece razonable y la "
"vara está bastante baja.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*chuckles.  \"Lucky for me then it doesn't matter if you believe me.  I do "
"gotta say though, it's funny you and I, a pair of actual real-live zombie "
"hunters, are talking face to face and you think my *survival story* is the "
"unlikely thing.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe por lo bajo. \"Por suerte no importa si me creés o no. Tengo que "
"decir, eso sí, que es gracioso que vos y yo, un par de cazadores de zombis "
"verdaderos, estemos hablando cara a cara y vos pienses que mi *historia de "
"supervivencia* es una cosa bastante improbable.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*glances your way, then makes eye contact as you move closer to speak.  He "
"is a strong-looking man in his mid forties, his hair greying and his face "
"flecked with stubble and travel dust.  The clothes he's wearing are clearly "
"scavenged, though they fit well, and he has the build of someone who until "
"recently had the luxury of carrying a few extra pounds.  \"Hi there.\"  He "
"presents his hand to shake.  \"You don't look like you belong here.  Name's "
"Bailey, John Bailey.\""
msgstr ""
"*mira hacia tu lado, luego hace contacto visual mientras te acercás para "
"hablar. Es un hombre fuerte a mitad de sus cuarenta años, con su pelo "
"encanecido y su cara manchada con barba y polvo. Tiene ropa que claramente "
"encontró por ahí pero le queda bien, y tiene la estructura de una persona "
"que hasta hace poco tenía el lujo de llevar unos kilitos de más. \"Hola, "
"che.\" Extiende su mano para saludar. \"No parece que fueras de este lugar. "
"Mi nombre es Bailey, John Bailey.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*laughs a bit sheepishly.  \"Seems distasteful to keep track of that stuff, "
"doesn't it?\"  He touches a series of notches on his <mywp>.  \"I'm human "
"though.  I'm up to <npc_val:zkc_john> so far.  Seems like a lot to me, "
"especially since I try to avoid actually engaging the enemy if I can help "
"it.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe un poco tímidamente. \"Parece de mal gusto tener registro de eso, "
"¿no te parece?\" Toca una serie de muescas en su <mywp>. \"Pero soy humano, "
"eh. Estoy por los <npc_val:zkc_john> por ahora. Parece mucho para mí, "
"especialmente porque intento evitar enfrentarme al enemigo si puedo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*nods as you approach, then smiles and stretches casually.  \"Anything I can"
" do for you, friend?\""
msgstr ""
"*asiente cuando te acercás, después sonríe y se estira. \"¿Puedo hacer algo "
"por vos, amigo?\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*raises an eyebrow.  \"I don't know about that.  You should be careful about"
" thinking people who don't make the same choices as you are inferior.  Sure,"
" not everyone's suited to scavenge, but a scavenger's got to have a safe "
"home, too.\""
msgstr ""
"*levanta una ceja. \"No sé. Tendrías que tener cuidado con eso de pensar que"
" los que no toman las mismas decisiones que vos son personas inferiores. Sí,"
" no todos están capacitados para cartonear pero un cartonero también tiene "
"que tener un lugar seguro.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*rubs his stubble, looking thoughtful.  \"I agree it's important to be "
"independent, but don't forget, working together is what makes us better than"
" the undead.  It's how we got out of the trees and fields, and into "
"civilization.  Anyway, I don't want to talk philosophy at you.  If you're "
"doing well on your own, more power to you!\""
msgstr ""
"*se toca la barba, como pensando. \"Estoy de acuerdo con que es importante "
"ser independiente pero no te olvides, trabajar en grupo es lo que nos hace "
"mejores que los muertos vivos. Es por eso que salimos de los árboles y los "
"campos y fuimos hacia la civilización. Pero de todas maneras, no quiero "
"hablar de filosofía. Si vos estás bien solo, ¡más poder para vos!\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"*sizes you up and down, and shakes his head sadly.  \"Darius and I have a "
"good thing going, and a third person would be hard to justify, especially "
"these days.  Trust comes hard.  I'm sorry.  I hope you've got someone to "
"watch your back, but it can't be me.\""
msgstr ""
"*te evalúa de arriba abajo y mueve su cabeza tristemente. \"Darius y yo "
"tenemos algo bueno funcionando y una tercera persona sería difícil de "
"justificar, especialmente por estos días. La confianza es difícil. Lo "
"lamento. Espero que tengas alguien que te cuide la espalda pero no puedo ser"
" yo.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Are you looking for work?"
msgstr "¿Estás buscando trabajo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Can you give me any advice?"
msgstr "¿Me podés dar algún consejo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Damn straight.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Exactamente. La gente debería aprender a defenderse por sí sola."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Fuck that.  People should learn to fend for themselves."
msgstr "Un carajo. La gente debería aprender a defenderse por sí sola."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Got time to teach me anything?"
msgstr "¿Tenés tiempo para enseñarme algo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John, I'm afraid I can't stay to talk."
msgstr "Hola, John. Lamento no poder quedarme a conversar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Hi John.  What are you doing here?"
msgstr "Hola, John. ¿Qué hacés acá?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "How did you know things were going to go wrong?"
msgstr "¿Cómo sabías que las cosas iban a salir mal?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Huh, well, the short story is, I got my wife and kids out of town in the "
"really, really early days.  She's got great intuition for stuff and when she"
" told me to get ready to leave town, I figured at worst we'd have an "
"unnecessary early spring vacation in my dad's old cabin, you know?  "
"Obviously, turns out trusting her gut saved us all and then some.  Things "
"were still tough, but from what I've heard, I might be the only person left "
"on the Eastern Seaboard who still has his whole nuclear family.  Still got a"
" lot of survivor's guilt for that… still lost everyone else.  Anyway, one "
"thing led to another and we gathered a few other people that we watch out "
"for.  My man Darius, he joined up early on and he and I do the scouting and "
"scavenging and watch each others' backs."
msgstr ""
"Eh, bueno, la versión corta es que salí con mi esposa y mis hijos del pueblo"
" muy al comienzo de todo. Ella tiene muy buena intuición para las cosas y "
"cuando me dijo que me preparara para salir del pueblo, me imaginé que como "
"mucho eran unas vacaciones innecesarias y tempranas de primavera en la vieja"
" cabaña de mi padre, ¿entendés? Obviamente, resultó que confiar en su "
"intuición nos salvó. Las cosas siguieron siendo difíciles pero por lo que "
"escuché, puede que haya sido la única persona con la familia entera en toda "
"la costa este. Igual tengo mucho culpa de sobreviviente por eso… y perdí a "
"todos los demás. De todos modos, una cosa llevó a la otra y nos juntamos con"
" otra gente con la que nos cuidamos. Mi amigo Darius se unió al principio y "
"con él hacemos la exploración y el cartoneo y cuidamos las espaldas de los "
"demás."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I could use someone like you.  Want to travel with me?"
msgstr "Me vendría bien estar con alguien como vos. ¿Querés viajar conmigo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I do odd jobs if people need help.  Not on a volunteer basis you understand,"
" but I try not to be unfair about it either.  Lots of people need a bit of "
"help these days, often just with little things a scavenger like me can find "
"for them.  It's easy for folks like you and me to underestimate how scared a"
" lot of people are to go back out in that place.  The situation's bad enough"
" as it is, but these kind of people took refuge back when it was true chaos "
"out there.  Lots of trauma to unpack there.  Anyway, if there's little "
"things I can do for them, I try to help where I can, so long as it doesn't "
"put me in too much danger."
msgstr ""
"Hago trabajos raros si la gente necesita ayuda. No como voluntario, viste, "
"pero trato de no ser injusto tampoco. Mucha gente necesita un poco de ayuda "
"por estos días, a menudo es suficiente con lo poco que puede encontrar un "
"cartonero como yo. Es fácil para la gente como vos y yo subestimar qué tanto"
" miedo de volver a ese lugar tienen las personas. La situación es "
"suficientemente mala pero este tipo de personas se refugiaron cuando comenzó"
" el verdadero caos. Muchos traumas para establecerse ahí. De todas maneras, "
"si hay alguna cosita que pueda hacer por ellos, intento ayudar cuando puedo,"
" siempre que no me ponga en peligro."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I don't know, the zombies sure seem to work together to me."
msgstr "No sé, a mí me parece que los zombis trabajan en grupo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I don't really know.  Food stocks aren't too bad for me and mine, I found a "
"stock of canned goods early on that will last us for a while yet.  I don't "
"use a gun if I can avoid it, too noisy.  I notice these guys seem to keep a "
"lot of building supplies though, and trying to get a vehicle downtown to "
"loot a hardware store or a lumberyard is suicide, so I think that's where "
"they're going to get my money.  I wonder if they deliver."
msgstr ""
"La verdad que no sé. El suministro de comida no está tan mal para los míos, "
"encontré comida enlatada que nos va a durar por un tiempo. No uso armas si "
"lo puedo evitar, hacen demasiado ruido. Vi que estos tipos parecían tener "
"muchos materiales de construcción e intentar conseguir un vehículo para "
"saquear una ferretería o una maderera es suicida, así que pensé que ahí era "
"donde podía conseguir mi plata. Me pregunto si hacen envíos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I might take you up on that, but for now I've gotta go."
msgstr "Podría aceptar la oferta pero ahora me tengo que ir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"I'll be straight with you, I don't want to tell you too much about my "
"people, okay?  You seem all right, don't get me wrong, but I've seen some "
"scary fuckin' people out there, who come on all normal and then try to bite "
"your face off when they get you alone.  Everyone's reaction to the world's "
"end is a bit different.  Things are stable with my people now, but we don't "
"really welcome new faces anymore.  I wish it weren't that way.  Maybe if you"
" and I get to know each other better some day, I'll change my mind."
msgstr ""
"Te voy a ser sincero, no te quiero decir mucho acerca de mi gente, "
"¿entendés? No es por vos, no me malinterpretes, pero conocí gente bastante "
"siniestra dando vueltas que vienen todo normalitos y después intentan "
"arrancarte la cara de un tarascó cuando pueden. Es diferente la reacción de "
"cada uno frente al fin del mundo. Las cosas están bien ahora entre mi gente "
"pero ya no recibimos personas nuevas. Me gustaría que no tuviera que ser de "
"esa manera. Tal vez si nos conocemos mejor, algún día cambie mi parecer."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "I'll bear that in mind.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Voy a tener eso en mente. ¿Qué me dijiste que hacías acá?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "It sounds like you have some past there.  You want to talk about it?"
msgstr "Pareciera que tenés una historia ahí. ¿Querés hablar sobre eso?"

#. ~ Unique name of an NPC
#. ~ A survivor who sometimes visits the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "John Bailey"
msgstr "John Bailey"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Let's change the subject.  What did you say you were doing here?"
msgstr "Vamos a cambiar de tema. ¿Qué me dijiste que hacías acá?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Move on\" where?"
msgstr "¿Te vas a dónde?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Nice talking to you, I've gotta go."
msgstr "Me gusta hablar con vos, ahora me tengo que ir."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Not at the moment, thanks."
msgstr "Por el momento no, gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Not really, no.  It's old stuff, and there's enough going on.  Let's just "
"say I'm no stranger to loss, either my own or others'."
msgstr ""
"La verdad que no. Lo pasado, pisado, y el presente es suficiente. Digamos "
"solamente que estoy acostumbrado a la pérdida, sea la propia o la de otros."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Oh, jeez, yeah.  The world really went to shit, didn't it?  Well, I've seen "
"some weird alien things.  Our rule is 'scared is better than dead'.  If we "
"don't know what something is and how to kill it, we steer wide and clear.  "
"One time I saw this flaming eyeball a long way off, I was scouting from a "
"cell phone tower.  It made eye contact with me and I just started "
"hallucinating shit.  Darius stopped me from falling right off the tower.  "
"Stuff like that is why I think you have to be a bit off your rocker to "
"travel these days unless you have no choice.  Anything we don't know, we "
"turn around and pedal hard.  So far, we haven't met anything our bikes can't"
" outrun."
msgstr ""
"Ah, mierda, sí. El mundo se fue al carajo en serio, ¿no? Bueno, vi algunas "
"cosas raras extraterrestres. Nuestra regla es 'mejor asustado que muerto'. "
"Si no sabemos qué es y cómo matarlo, nos mantenemos alejados. Una vez vimos "
"un ojo llameante a lo lejos, yo estaba mirando desde una torre de telefonía "
"celular. Hizo contacto visual conmigo y yo empecé a alucinar cosas raras. "
"Darius evitó que me cayera de la torre. Las cosas como esa son las que me "
"hacen pensar que tenés que estar un poco mal del balero para viajar en estos"
" tiempos, salvo que no tengas otra opción. Cualquier cosa que no conozcamos,"
" damos la vuelta y pedaleamos fuerte. Hasta ahora, no nos cruzamos con nada "
"que sea más rápido que nuestras bicicletas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "On your way\" where?"
msgstr "¿Tu camino a dónde?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"People should learn to fend for themselves, not just get you to hand "
"everything to them."
msgstr ""
"La gente tiene que aprender a defenderse por sí sola, y no esperar que vos "
"les des todo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Same as you, I imagine,\" John shrugs.  \"Checking "
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sometimes, I kinda wonder why other people *didn't* know things were going "
"to go wrong.  Hindsight is twenty-twenty, I guess.  I'll be honest though, "
"as much as I'd like to pat myself on the back, it wasn't me that figured it "
"out.  When the really early riots started out, even though they were way up "
"in the Midwest, my wife just had a bad feeling.  We'd been thinking of a "
"getaway anyway, and I had some time off, so we took it as an excuse to get "
"out to the cabin and wait for everything to blow over.  Here we are.  It "
"wasn't so much knowing how things were going to go, more just straight luck "
"that we trusted our - *her* - gut at the right time and lucked out."
msgstr ""
"A veces, me pregunto por qué otra gente *no sabía* que todo iba a salir mal."
" Pero es fácil con el diario del lunes, supongo. Para ser honesto, por mucho"
" que quiera felicitarme a mí mismo, yo no fui el que se dio cuenta. Cuando "
"empezaron los primeros disturbios, incluso aunque fueron bastante lejos en "
"el oeste, mi señora tuvo un mal presentimiento. Igual ya estábamos pensando "
"en irnos y yo tenía un poco de tiempo libre, así que lo usamos como excusa "
"para ir a la cabaña y esperar que todo explotara. Y acá estamos. No sabíamos"
" qué iba a pasar, fue más bien suerte que confiamos en su instinto en ese "
"momento y tuvimos suerte."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sorry, but that's all I have time for at the moment.  Darius is waiting "
"outside."
msgstr "Perdón pero no tengo más tiempo ahora. Darius está afuera esperando."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sounds about the same as me, yep.  I'd better get back to it."
msgstr "Parece lo mismo que yo, sí. Mejor vuelvo a eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Sure, I guess.  I don't know if I know anything you don't, you seem like you"
" can handle yourself.  I've made it this far by not engaging whenever "
"possible.  I'm never going to kill all the zombies out there.  Darius and I "
"try not to fight if we can avoid it, and if we can't, we try to always have "
"the advantage.  Numbers, weaponry, terrain.  Zombies are clumsy and stupid "
"so we lead them across bushes and things to trip and stumble.  We take high "
"ground and let them plough into ladders like idiots while we stick 'em with "
"spears from above.  Mostly, though, we try not to be seen.  We use bikes "
"instead of cars because they don't make noise and don't need gas, plus we "
"can take forest trails and things and avoid traffic jams.  Those things are "
"suicide.  We try to avoid the cities, and when we do go close, we stick to "
"the outskirts and raid the outlying houses.  In those, we keep crouched and "
"try to get deep into the building fast, or down into the basement, so that "
"little noises don't carry much and nothing from outside can see us.  Also, "
"zombies being idiots, closing the blinds is a great move.  I always keep a "
"crowbar for opening doors and windows, but I try not to use it if I can "
"avoid it.  Darius can pick locks, which is slower but doesn't make noise.  "
"We get a lot more mileage from raiding gas stations and other rural sites, "
"where if there are a few zombies, we can usually lead them away."
msgstr ""
"Seguro, creo. No sé si sé algo que vos no sepas, tenés pinta de saber "
"manejarte. Sobreviví hasta ahora esquivando todo en la medida de lo posible."
" Nunca voy a poder matar a todos los zombis que andan por ahí. Darius y yo "
"tratamos de evitar el enfrentamiento y si no podemos, intentamos tener "
"siempre la ventaja. Cantidad, armas, terreno. Los zombis son torpes y "
"estúpidos así que los llevamos hacia los arbustos y cosas que los hagan "
"tropezar y caerse. Los esperamos en terreno elevado y los dejamos apilarse "
"en escaleras como idiotas mientras los atacamos con lanzas desde arriba. "
"Pero mayormente tratamos de que no nos vean. Usamos bicicleta en lugar de "
"autos porque no hacen ruido y no necesitan combustible, y además podemos "
"pasar por caminos en bosques y evitar los embotellamientos. Es casi un "
"suicidio andar en auto. Intentamos evitar las ciudades y cuando nos "
"acercamos, nos mantenemos por la parte externa saqueando las casas. Y "
"adentro de las casas nos mantenemos agachados y tratamos de meternos rápido "
"lejos de las aberturas o en el sótano, para que los ruidos no atraigan nada "
"de afuera que nos pudiera ver. Además, como los zombis son idiotas, cerrar "
"las cortinas es una buena idea. Siempre llevo una barreta para abrir puertas"
" o ventanas pero trato de no usarla si no es necesario. Darius puede abrir "
"cerraduras, es más lento pero no hace ruido. Sacamos mucho provecho de las "
"estaciones de servicio y de otros sitios rurales, donde si hay zombis los "
"podemos guiar hacia otro lado."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Sure, let's talk trade."
msgstr "Seguro, hablemos de negocios."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Talk to Darius if you want to know about Darius.  He's a good man, and he "
"won't bite-- ugh, sorry, that's a turn of phrase we should probably retire, "
"hey?  Anyway.  I don't know if we'd have made it through the first days "
"without him.  He gets a bit jumpy around crowds since the riots though, so "
"he's out watching our stuff."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Tell me about Darius."
msgstr "Contame acerca de Darius."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Thanks, I'll think about it.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "Gracias, voy a pensarlo. ¿Qué estabas diciendo antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That is one hell of a life.  You must have some useful skills to teach."
msgstr ""
"Esa es una vida extraordinaria. Debés tener algunas habilidades útiles para "
"enseñar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "That seems like a pretty unlikely story."
msgstr "Eso parece una historia bastante improbable."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a shame.  We'd be a good team.  People like you and I are made of "
"stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"Qué lástima. Seríamos un buen equipo. La gente como vos y yo estamos hechos "
"de materia fuerte."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's a tougher question than you might think.  I've had quite the life.  "
"My dad was a mechanic, and when I was young I used to help around the shop "
"quite a bit.  I started out thinking I was going to get into that line of "
"work, but then I got sidetracked and wound up getting into computers and "
"electrical work for a long time.  Did part of an electrical engineering "
"degree, then decided it wasn't for me and quit that.  Spent a bit of time "
"doing freelance electrical and programming work, then got recruited by a "
"startup that was designing and programming medical equipment.  I was "
"supposed to be a general technician, but through a weird series of events I "
"wound up in sales, then management.  I hated management, and I'd made a big "
"nest egg from my share stock, so I cashed out and tried to retire young.  "
"That was a dumb move, I was bored as hell, so I finished off my degree and "
"started doing on-call teaching work for shop, computers, math, and things "
"like that at a college and high school level.  Just part time, and I spent "
"the rest of my time outdoors, hiking and whatnot."
msgstr ""
"Esa es una pregunta más difícil de lo que pensás. Tuve una buena vida. Mi "
"papá era mecánico y cuando era pibe lo ayudaba bastante en el negocio. "
"Empecé a pensar que me iba a quedar en ese rubro pero me desvié y terminé "
"metiéndome en computación y electrónica por mucho tiempo. Hice parte de la "
"carrera de ingeniería electrónica y después decidí que no era para mí y la "
"dejé. Estuve un tiempo haciendo trabajos electrónicos y de programación, "
"después me contrataron para una empresa nueva que estaba diseñando y "
"programando equipamiento médico. Se suponía que yo era técnico general pero "
"por una serie rara de eventos terminé en ventas, y después en la gerencia. "
"Odiaba estar en gerencia y había juntado unos ahorros, así que vendí mis "
"acciones e intenté jubilarme joven. Eso fue una mala idea, me aburría como "
"la mierda así que terminó la carrera y empecé a enseñar comercio, "
"informática, matemática y cosas así en la universidad y en secundaria. Pero "
"media jornada y pasaba el resto afuera, en excursiones y caminatas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"That's for the weaklings.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"Eso es para los debiluchos. La gente como vos y yo estamos hechos de materia"
" fuerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What about things other than zombies?"
msgstr "¿Y qué onda con las otras cosas, las cosas que no son zombis?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What are you shopping for?"
msgstr "¿Qué andás comprando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What did you used to do before?"
msgstr "¿Y antes a qué te dedicabas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What do you know about this place?"
msgstr "¿Qué sabés de este lugar?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "What kind of work are you looking for?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de trabajo estás buscando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you guys located?  Can I join up too?"
msgstr "¿Dóndes están ubicados? ¿Puedo unirme a ustedes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Where are you headed next?"
msgstr "¿Y después para dónde vas?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Who can say, really?  I don't really have a strong plan.  Depends on how "
"this trip goes.  Once my vehicle is full up, I'll have to head back to my "
"hideout and check on everyone there.  I don't like being gone too long."
msgstr ""
"¿Quién podría decirlo, no? La verdad es que no tengo un plan fuerte. Depende"
" de cómo vaya el viaje. Cuando mi vehículo esté lleno, voy a volver a mi "
"escondite y ver cómo andan todos. No me gusta irme por mucho tiempo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"everyone\"?"
msgstr "¿Quiénes son todos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Who is \"you and yours\"?"
msgstr "¿Quiénes son \"los tuyos\"?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, I, uh… I know a bit about that stuff.  Hard not to empathize, "
"especially when I know I'm not quite as hard as others, by sheer luck.  "
"Besides, there are so few of us left now.  What's the point in wasting time "
"judging other people for how hard they took the end of the world?"
msgstr ""
"Sí, yo, eh… conozco un poco sobre eso. Es difícil no sentir empatía, "
"especialmente cuando sé que no soy tan duro como otros, de pura suerte. "
"Además, quedamos tan pocos de nosotros ahora. ¿Para qué gastar tiempo "
"juzgando a otras personas sobre su manera de recibir el fin del mundo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You look like you can handle yourself in a fight.  What's your zombie kill "
"count?"
msgstr ""
"Tenés la apariencia de alguien que se maneja bien en las peleas. ¿Cuántos "
"zombis mataste?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You looking for any kind of work?"
msgstr "¿Estás buscando algún trabajo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "You seem to know a lot about how people feel."
msgstr "Parece que sabés mucho sobre cómo se siente la gente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You'd do better to talk to the people here about it.  Seems like a bunch of "
"them gathered here in the early days of <the_cataclysm> and managed to make "
"it through.  It's the biggest bunch of survivors I've found yet, but most of"
" them hunker up in the basement.  I can understand the urge.  We've all been"
" through way too much.  They say they don't have room for more people "
"though, so I'm just here to do some shopping, see if there's work to be "
"done, then move on."
msgstr ""
"Te conviene hablar con la gente de acá sobre eso. Parece como si un grupo se"
" reunió acá en los primeros días del <the_cataclysm> y lograron sobrevivir. "
"Es el grupo más grande de sobrevivientes que encontré por ahora pero la "
"mayoría está refugiado en el sótano. Puedo entender la necesidad. Todos "
"hemos pasado por muchas cosas jodidas. Dicen que no tienen lugar para más "
"gente así que solo vengo a comprar cosas, ver si necesitan algún trabajo y "
"después me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"You've got that right.  People like you and I are made of stronger stuff."
msgstr ""
"En eso tenés razón. La gente como vos y yo estamos hechos de materia fuerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid "Your whole story seems a bit unlikely."
msgstr "Toda tu historia parece poco probable."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/john_bailey.json
msgid ""
"the place out, doing a little shopping.  Then I'll be on my way again.  "
"Might see if they have any work that needs done first, if the price is "
"right."
msgstr ""
"el lugar, buscando algo para comprar. Después voy a seguir mi camino. Por "
"ahí miro a ver si tienen algún trabajo para ofrecerme, por el precio "
"adecuado."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Actually, I think I'm on the right track here, but you might have some luck "
"finding a little something something back at the Free Merchant base.  They "
"seemed pretty desperate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Any progress on getting to the camp?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to that FEMA camp?  I want to go there too if "
"it's so great."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Can you give me directions to where you're going too?  I love cartography."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Everything is going to be all right."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Good luck with that.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"Here, I'll mark it on your map.  I wouldn't bet they'll treat you any "
"differently than us though.  You might try and bring something to trade, "
"they like that."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Hey man.  Do you have any heroin?  I'm in a bit of a bind."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I can't tell if you're joking or not, please don't say such things."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I don't have time for zombie bait like you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I haven't been to any refugee center.  Can you tell me where it is?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I love you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I think you might need it even more than me.  Here you go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
"I'm a refugee, but don't get the wrong idea.  I've got big dreams of "
"settling down after this and starting a big family.  I just need to find the"
" right place and the right person.  Last couple of places didn't work out so"
" well."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I should be going before I do something bad again."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Looking good there.  I like your whole setup.  What's your story?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Never, that heroin is for me and me alone."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nice.  Good to see you again.  What do you want from me?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No thank you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No worries friend, good luck to you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "No, I don't have any."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"No, I'm not really with them.  We just got stuck together in the same messed"
" up evacuation place.  This one guy was really nice, but they wouldn't let "
"us stay.  They got there first so they told us we needed to find our own "
"place, but if we got anything they wanted they'd trade some of the stuff "
"they have.  I tried to talk them into helping but they were so cold to me."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Not interested.  I'd better get going."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Nothing, just saying hi."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course, we're all in this together.  Let me mark that on your map."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Of course.  How do I get there?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, I wasn't joking <name_b>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Oh, uh, thanks.  I guess."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Please don't hurt us, we're just trying to get to safety."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "So you're not attached right now?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Such a disappointment…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the information.  I'd better go."
msgstr "Gracias por la información. Mejor me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Thanks for the story.  I'd better go."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "The hard part is getting there."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Things must be better at the camp…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "This is the beginning of a beautiful thing.  I'm with you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We were at the same little evacuation hut, but it was all messed up, just "
"used condoms and broken bottles and lipstick writing on the walls.  We found"
" another group of refugees like us on the road, but they had all been "
"killed, all ripped up, blood everywhere.  We took their food and made it all"
" the way to a big refugee center, but somebody there with a gun told us "
"there was no room, so we're going to a FEMA camp.  They should have more "
"room and supplies.  No guarantees, but it's a chance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "We're all in this together, looking forward to meeting you there."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"We're just trying to find a safe place right now.  I think there's a FEMA "
"camp nearby that should have room for us."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Reach FEMA Camp"
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Well, success I guess."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid ""
"What if I want to hurt you?  I'm so good at it and I've had so much "
"practice."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "What's your situation here?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Why, where were you before?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yeah, I guess it's hard all over.  I'd better get going."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yes!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "Yes.  I'll be on my way then."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid "You again.  Any good news?  Haven't heard any in a long time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Affirmative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should come with me instead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Negative response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "You should definitely come with me instead."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name suffix of an NPC
#. ~ Random NPC, can direct you to the free merchants and nearest FEMA camp.
#. ~ Random NPC, can be recruited away.
#. ~ Random NPC, demands heroin and can accept.
#: data/json/npcs/random_encounters/refugee_caravans.json
msgid "refugee"
msgstr "refugiado"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ", but I'm so hungry."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "All right!  Let's get going."
msgstr "¡Está bien! Vamos yendo."

#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#. ~ All the beggars have been camping inside the evac shelter because they're
#. too weak and unskilled to make it on their own.
#. ~ This is the only beggar with some skills, sort of the leader.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_5_Yusuke_Taylor.json
msgid "Beggar"
msgstr "Mendigo"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Can I ask you something else first?"
msgstr "¿Te puedo preguntar algo antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Come with me.  Maybe you're not the greatest adventurer, but it's better "
"than living here."
msgstr ""
"Vení conmigo. Tal vez no sos el mejor aventurero, pero es mejor que vivir "
"acá."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "Get away from me."
msgstr "Salí de acá."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "Here, you can have this <topic_item>."
msgstr "Tomá, te podés quedar con este/a <topic_item>."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Hey, here, I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "Hey, acá, tal vez tenga algo de comida para vos. Dejame ver."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I can keep you safe.  I'll take you there myself."
msgstr "Yo te puedo mantener a salvo. Te voy a llevar personalmente ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe they can't use your skills "
"here, but I could."
msgstr ""
"Tengo un campamento propio, un poco lejos de acá. Tal vez acá no tengan "
"interés por tus habilidades, pero yo sí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  Maybe you can't scavenge, but we "
"can use any warm bodies that can lift a tool.  You'd be safer and better fed"
" there."
msgstr ""
"Tengo un campamento propio, un poco lejos de acá. Tal vez no puedas "
"cartonear pero nos viene bien cualquier cuerpo que pueda agarrar una "
"herramienta. Vas a estar más seguro y mejor alimentado ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I have a camp of my own, away from here.  You could come there.  There "
"aren't many people left, we could use anyone regardless of skills."
msgstr ""
"Tengo un campamento propio, un poco lejos de acá. Podés ir ahí. No quedan "
"muchas personas, nos vendría bien cualquiera sin importar tus habilidades."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I hope you'll reconsider eventually.  Bye."
msgstr "Espero que lo pienses mejor alguna vez. Chau."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I might have some food for you.  Let me check."
msgstr "Tal vez tenga algo de comida para vos. Dejame ver."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I really appreciate everything you've done for me, but I don't think you get"
" it.  I can't go out there.  I will die.  I know it's horrible camping out "
"here, but I just can't face that nightmare again."
msgstr ""
"Realmente agradezco lo que hiciste por mí, pero no creo que entiendas. No "
"puedo salir. Me voy a morir. Sé que es horrible acampar ahí afuera, pero no "
"puedo enfrentarme a esa pesadilla otra vez."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"I was a high school math teacher.  It was a good job, I loved it.  Funny "
"enough, it's not super applicable after the end of the world.  I mean, at "
"some point people are going to need a teacher again, but right now they just"
" want food, shelter, and clothing."
msgstr ""
"Era profesor de matemática en una escuela. Era un lindo trabajo, me "
"encantaba. Lo gracioso es que no es muy útil para el fin del mundo. Quiero "
"decir, en algún momento los profesores serán necesarios otra vez, pero ahora"
" solo se busca comida, refugio y ropa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr "Perdoname, no te puedo ayudar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I was wrong.  I can't help you."
msgstr "Lo lamento, me equivoqué. No tengo nada."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I'm sorry, I'm too hungry to make a big decision like that."
msgstr ""
"Lo lamento, tengo demasiado hambre como para tomar una decisión tan "
"importante como esa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "I've got some more food, if you want it."
msgstr "Tengo un poco más de comida si querés."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_4_Brandon_Garder.json
msgid ""
"I've talked to the others, and they're all willing to come.  So, you joining"
" us?"
msgstr "Hablé con los otros y todos desean venir. Así que, ¿te vas a unir?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_3_Luo_Meizhen.json
msgid "Let's talk about something else then."
msgstr "Hablemos de otra cosa entonces."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_2_Dino_Dave.json
msgid "No problem.  Bye."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK, I'll talk to them too."
msgstr "OK, voy a hablar con ellos también."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "OK.  For now let's talk about something else."
msgstr "OK. Ahora, hablemos de otra cosa."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"Out there?  That's suicide!  People that go out there don't come back, "
"people who can hold their own… unlike me.  I'd rather take my chances "
"begging for scraps and waiting for someone in the center to die and make "
"room for me, thanks."
msgstr ""
"¿Por ahí? ¡Es suicidio! La gente que sale no vuelve, gente que puede "
"manejarse… no como yo. Prefiero quedarme mendigando y esperando que alguien "
"en el centro se muera y haya lugar para mí. Gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Please, help me.  I need food."
msgstr "Por favor, ayudame. Necesito comida."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Reena Sandhu"
msgstr "Reena Sandhu"

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Hungry beggar in the refugee center.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Teacher"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "Thank you so much."
msgstr "Muchas gracias."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"That's a kind offer of you, but I think I'd rather take my chances here than"
" risking it out there again.  I remember <the_cataclysm>, I'm not in any "
"hurry to face that again."
msgstr ""
"Es una oferta interesante pero creo que prefiero quedarme acá que "
"arriesgarme allá afuera otra vez. Me acuerdo del <the_cataclysm>, no tengo "
"ningún apuro en enfrentarme de nuevo a eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid ""
"They won't let me in.  They say they're too full.  I'm allowed to camp out "
"here as long as I keep it clean and don't make a fuss"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of effect type "Full"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This beggar in the refugee center has had something to eat recently."
msgstr ""
"Este mendigo en el centro de refugiados tuvo algo para comer recientemente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgid "This is wonderful of you, I really appreciate it."
msgstr "Maravilloso de tu parte, te lo agradezco mucho."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/beggars/BEGGAR_1_Reena_Sandhu.json
msgctxt "u:f"
msgid ""
"Well… you have shown that you can survive out there, and you've been able to"
" provide food, so I know you're thriving more than we are here.  All right, "
"I'll tell you what.  I'm not going anywhere without my friends here, we've "
"been through way too much together.  If you can convince Luo, Brandon, and "
"Yusuke to come along, then I'll go."
msgstr ""
"Bueno… has demostrado que podés sobrevivir acá, y fuiste capaz de proveer "
"comida, así que sé que estás progresando más que nosotros acá. Está bien, te"
" voy a decir algo. No voy a ninguna parte sin mis amigos, hemos pasado "
"muchas cosas juntos. Si podés convencer a Luo, Brandon y Yusuke de que "
"también se unan, voy."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
