msgid ""
"Hmm, well it is not ideal but I appreciate you trying and being willing to "
"help.  I will have to do my best despite the bad memories.  Thank you, my "
"friend."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I am afraid I cannot teach you right now.  Not only do I have no shop, but I"
" do not think I am in a good place for anything so taxing."
msgstr ""
"Lamentablemente, no puedo enseñarte en este momento. No solamente no tengo "
"taller, tampoco creo estar en un buen momento para algo tan agotador."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I could talk forever, but it's hard to make the words come.  He was so "
"*smart*.  Always on the computer, writing stories and programming silly "
"games in Scratch.  He had a little robotics toy he made walk around and do "
"funny dances.  It was a challenge to make him play with his friends "
"sometimes, he would get so far into himself and buried in that thing.  So "
"tough to be a parent, you know?  It is good for him to write, to learn, but "
"he also needs to socialize and have friends.  He'll grow out… he…"
msgstr ""
"Podría hablar por horas pero es difícil hacer que vengan las palabras. Él "
"era muy *inteligente*. Siempre en la computadora, escribiendo historias y "
"programando juegos tontos en Scratch. Había hecho un juguetito robótico que "
"caminaba y hacía unos bailes graciosos. Era un desafío hacerlo jugar con sus"
" amigos a veces, se ensimismaba y se encerraba en esa cosa. Difícil ser "
"padre, ¿viste? Es bueno para él escribir, aprender, pero también necesita "
"socializar y tener amigos. Va a crecer… él…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Stan_Borichenko.json
msgid "I just wanted to say hi.  I'll be on my way."
msgstr "Solo pasaba a saludar. Me voy yendo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I know it is a hard thing to hope, but were you able to find Ash's laptop?"
msgstr ""
"Ya sé que es difícil de esperar, pero ¿pudiste encontrar la notebook de Ash?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I see….  Well I shall get things in order!"
msgstr "Comprendo… ¡Bueno, voy a empezar a solucionar las cosas!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I was a carpenter.  I like to keep my hands busy, especially when I am "
"stressed.  Now, here I am, picking my nose and stuck thinking about my "
"problems and all that I've lost."
msgstr ""
"Era carpintera. Me gusta tener las manos ocupadas, especialmente cuando "
"estoy estresada. Ahora, acá estoy, metiéndome el dedo en la nariz y "
"empantanada pensando en mis problemas y todo lo que perdí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I would rather talk about what I have left: my husband, Stan, and his "
"brother Garry, my best friend.  Without them, I'd be lost myself.  What "
"we've lost is more than anyone should have to think about."
msgstr ""
"Prefiero hablar sobre lo que todavía tengo: mi marido, Stan, y su hermano "
"Garry, mi mejor amigo. Sin ellos, estaría perdida. Lo que hemos perdido es "
"más de lo que uno debiera pensar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'd better get going.  Let's do this later."
msgstr "Mejor me voy yendo. Hagamos esto después."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"I'm just a traveler, taking the chance to have some living human company.  "
"What's up in your life these days?"
msgstr ""
"Solo soy un viajante, tomando mi oportunidad de vivir en compañía humana. "
"¿Cómo va tu vida por estos días?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm so sorry, man.  Let's talk about something else."
msgstr "Lo lamento, che. Hablemos de otra cosa."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  Tell me more about Ash."
msgstr "Lamento tu pérdida. Contame un poco más sobre Ash."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm sorry.  I'd better get going."
msgstr "Lo lamento. Mejor me voy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm sorry.  What were you saying before?"
msgstr "Lo lamento. ¿Qué estabas diciendo antes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "I'm sure there's someone.  Would you like me to ask around?"
msgstr "Seguro que alguien puede. ¿Querés que vaya a preguntar?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "Is there anything I can help you out with?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo con lo que te pueda ayudar?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "Is there anything more I can do to help?"
msgstr "¿Hay algo más que pueda hacer para ayudar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
