msgctxt "u:n"
msgid "It is good to see you again, my friend."
msgstr "Qué bueno verte de nuevo, amigo mío."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "It is nice to meet you too.  To what do I owe the pleasure?"
msgstr "También es un gusto para mí. ¿A qué debo el placer?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"It is not hard to find.  I have even seen them for sale at the merchants, "
"but they save them as trade goods and will not give me as a gift."
msgstr ""
"No es tan difícil de encontrar. Algunos vendedores la tienen para vender, "
"pero las guardan como mercadería y no me las quieren regalar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"It is so strange to see this again, like a little piece of my old life.  I "
"don't know if I can bring myself to read what's on it yet, but having this "
"piece of him is a great comfort."
msgstr ""
"Es tan raro volver a ver esto otra vez, como un pedacito de mi antigua vida."
" No sé si pueda ponerme a leer lo que está en ella, pero tener este "
"fragmento de él es un gran consuelo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"It seems like carpentry work would be something the Free Merchants need.  "
"Why are you so bored?"
msgstr ""
"Parece que el trabajo de carpintería sería algo que los Mercaderes Libres "
"necesitan. ¿Por qué estás tan aburrida?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"It was difficult at first, but yes, I did.  It hurts, but it is good.  I am "
"so proud of him.  Would you like to see some… some of what you brought me?"
msgstr ""
"Al principio fue difícil, pero sí, lo hice. Dolió pero está bien. Estoy muy "
"orgulloso de él. ¿Te gustaría ver algo… algo de lo que me trajiste?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris his son's lost writing."
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"My son, Ash, had a laptop on which he kept his writing.  If you can find it,"
" it would mean so much to me.  I will give you directions to the shelter "
"where he left it.  It was barely a shelter, broken and torn apart.  It "
"should just be on the floor where it was dropped."
msgstr ""
"Mi hijo, Ash, tenía una notebook en la que guardaba lo que escribía. Si "
"podés conseguirla, significaría mucho para mí. Te voy a indicar cómo llegar "
"al refugio donde la dejó. Casi que ya no era un refugio, todo roto y "
"destrozado. Debería estar en el suelo donde se cayó."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "Nice to meet you, Boris."
msgstr "Un gusto conocerte, Boris."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find someone to clean up the back bay."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring Boris a circular saw."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find reference material about air rifles for
#. Jenny."
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find an electric motor"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Bring back a 60 L metal tank"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find a gunsmithing textbook"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Jenny_Forcette.json
msgid "No worries.  Let me know if you want to try again."
msgstr "No hay problema. Avisame si querés volver a intentarlo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"No, not great.  Like all here, I have lost too much.  I do not feel I can "
"ever come back from it.  Can anyone be strong enough?"
msgstr ""
"No, no muy bien. Como todos acá, perdí mucho. No siento que pueda "
"recuperarme de eso. ¿Se puede ser lo suficientemente fuerte?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"No.  In the evacuation shelter, distracted by grief, I forgot it.  We were "
"rushed onto the bus so quickly, and… well, I don't remember much of that "
"time.  His work was all saved on the hard drive, we thought we could "
"download it from the cloud when we arrived but, well, there is no cloud now."
"  Even if there were, it would only have his writing, not his little games, "
"his silly voice recordings."
msgstr ""
"No. En el refugio de evacuación, distraído por el dolor, me lo olvidé. Nos "
"apuraron para subir al colectivo, y… bueno, no me acuerdo mucho de ese "
"momento. Su trabaja estaba todo guardado en un disco, pensamos que podríamos"
" descargarlo de la nube cuando llegamos pero, bueno, ya no hay nube. Y "
"aunque hubiera, solamente tendrías sus escritos, no sus jueguitos, ni sus "
"grabaciones tontas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "Not today, I have to get going.  Just glad I was able to help."
msgstr "Hoy no, me tengo que ir. Pero me alegra haber podido ayudar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"Now that things are cleaned up in the back, is there anything holding you "
"back from working?"
msgstr ""
"Ahora que ya está limpia la pieza de atrás, ¿hay algo que te impida estar "
"trabajando?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"Now that you've got your tools and shop set up, do you think you could teach"
" me a thing or two about construction?"
msgstr ""
"Ahora que tenés tus herramientas y estableciste un taller, ¿te parece que me"
" enseñés alguna cosa sobre construcción?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "OK, let's get to work."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"Of course, yes.  I know this, but it is not so easy, is it?  So many are "
"gone, and I do not know which of the two I would prefer, just yet."
msgstr ""
"Claro, sí. Ya sé pero no es tan fácil, ¿no? Murieron muchos y no sé cuál de "
"los dos prefiero, por ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid "Oh.  Right.  It's been a long apocalypse.  What were you saying?"
msgstr "Ah. Bueno. Ha sido un largo apocalipsis. ¿Qué estabas diciendo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_refugees/NPC_Boris_Borichenko.json
msgid ""
"So, have you had a chance to get that laptop working and look at it yet?"
msgstr "Así que, ¿tuviste tiempo para hacer andar la notebook y revisarla?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
