msgid ""
"I've seen my share of zombies, I'm one of the ones that's ready to take em "
"on.  Nothing more."
msgstr ""
"Vi bastantes zombis, soy uno de los que están preparados para enfrentarlos. "
"Nada más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
"I've seen my share of zombies, I'm one of the ones that's ready to take em "
"on.  Nothing more."
msgstr ""
"Vi bastantes zombis, soy uno de los que están preparados para enfrentarlos. "
"Nada más."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid "It's honest work, and now and then I get to take a zombie down."
msgstr ""
"Es un trabajo honesto, y de vez en cuando tengo que hacer cagar algún zombi."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
msgid "Keep civil or I'll bring the pain."
msgstr "Mantenete civilizado o te voy a causar dolor."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
#: data/json/npcs/tacoma_ranch/NPC_ranch_guard.json
msgid "Ma'am, you really shouldn't be traveling out there."
msgstr "Señora, no debería estar viajando por ahí afuera."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid "Nah."
msgstr "Nah."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid "No, sorry…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid "None of your business really, is it."
msgstr "Nada que tengas que saber, eso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Not unless you pay me.  Try the shopkeep, they can sell our services just "
"like anything else."
msgstr ""
"No, salvo que me pagues. Probá con los que tienen negocios, te pueden vender"
" nuestros servicios como cualquier otra cosa."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Nothing too fancy.  We have a rota of anyone able bodied that can handle "
"themselves."
msgstr ""
"Nada demasiado elegante. Tenemos una lista de tareas para cualquiera que "
"pueda manejarse."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Oh the helicopter?  Yeah, I tried finding the crash site around where the "
"guy said he heard the crash but I didn't find nothing."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Oh, yes, what a story, I almost wish I had been there to see it, almost."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Sure yeah, I remember, I was on caravan duty when I saw it, it got caught in"
" of those weird storms, as we started driving away I heard a big splash "
"sound."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Talk to one of the bosses about that.  You'd have to pay me to go back there"
" though, that's gonna be a hell of a job."
msgstr ""
"Hablá con uno de los jefes acerca de eso. Pero me vas a tener que pagar para"
" que vuelva ahí atrás, va a ser un trabajo de mierda."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"The crashed helicopter?  Eh, I'm pretty sure it's just a story, no one ever "
"found anything."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Yeah I was part of the caravan that spotted it, it was headed east then when"
" the storm broke out it got caught by some kind of creature, I heard "
"gunshots then it started flying down rapidly, I heard it crash but I'm not "
"sure where exactly."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"Yes I was told the story by the others, I'm glad I wasn't there though, I "
"hate those storms."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_free_merchant_guard_generic.json
msgid ""
"You know how it is, people talk, I mean sure, there was one of those weird "
"storms at the time but the helicopter story?  I don't believe it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Can I trade for supplies?"
msgstr "¿Podemos comerciar recursos?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Can't blame you, but come back if you change your mind."
msgstr "No te puedo culpar, pero volvé si cambiás de parecer."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
msgid "Citizen…"
msgstr "Ciudadano…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Do you provide medical services?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Download Encryption Codes"
msgstr "Descargar Códigos de Encriptación"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Download Research Archives"
msgstr "Descargar Archivos de Investigación"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Download Workstation Data"
msgstr "Descargar Información de Trabajo"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Excellent.  Take this blood draw kit; once you've found a zombie corpse, use"
" it to extract blood from the body, then take it to a hospital for analysis."
msgstr ""
"Excelente. Agarrá este equipo de extracción de sangre; una vez que tengas un"
" cadáver zombi, usalo para extraer sangre del cadáver, y luego llevalo al "
"hospital para hacer el análisis."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Expect the lab to be locked as usual."
msgstr "Acordate que el laboratorio va a estar cerrado, como es normal."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Fantastic!  I should be able to reconstruct what cargo moved between which "
"labs.  I wonder what was really going on down there."
msgstr ""
"¡Fantástico! Creo que puedo reconstruir qué cargamento fue trasladado entre "
"los laboratorios. Me pregunto qué estaba pasando ahí abajo."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Find Lab Tunnels"
msgstr "Encontrar Túneles de Laboratorio"

#. ~ Description of mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"First, you need to kill <color_light_blue>any zombie</color> and extract the blood from its body using the <color_light_blue>blood draw kit</color>.\n"
"Second, you need to deliver this blood to any working <color_light_blue>centrifuge with a computer</color>.  Equipment like this can most commonly be found at <color_light_blue>hospitals</color>, but you can also try to search for it at <color_light_blue>medical labs</color>.\n"
"Third, you need to place the extracted blood on the <color_light_blue>centrifuge</color> and analyze it using the <color_light_blue>computer nearby</color>.  If you're successful, the data will be written on an <color_light_blue>empty USB drive</color> you have to provide.\n"
"Finally, you need to bring the USB drive with the data back to the <color_light_blue>Doctor</color>."
msgstr ""
"Primero, necesitás matar <color_light_blue>cualquier zombi</color> y extraerle sangre del cuerpo usando un <color_light_blue>equipo de extracción de sangre</color>.\n"
"Segundo, tenés que encontrar cualquier <color_light_blue>centrifugadora con una computadora</color> que funcione. Este tipo de equipamiento pueden ser encontrado comúnmente en <color_light_blue>hospitales</color> pero también podés buscarla en <color_light_blue>laboratorios médicos</color>.\n"
"Tercero, necesitás poner la sangre extraída en la <color_light_blue>centrifugadora</color> y analizarla usando la <color_light_blue>computadora cercana</color>. Si todo sale bien, la información será escrita en un <color_light_blue>pendrive vacío</color> que tenés que llevar.\n"
"Finalmente, tenés que llevarle el pendrive con la información de vuelta al <color_light_blue>Doctor</color>."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Good luck with that…"
msgstr "Que tengas suerte con eso…"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Great!  I've mapped out a route to the address."
msgstr "¡Genial! Pude marcar la ruta hacia esa dirección."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Great!  I've mapped out a route, it should look like a normal house.  Bring "
"back anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"¡Genial! Pude marcar la ruta, debería parecer una casa normal. Traé en un "
"pendrive todo lo que encontrés."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Great!  I've mapped out a route.  Bundle up, it gets colder the deeper you "
"go and it looks like the archives were on the fourth basement level."
msgstr ""
"¡Genial! Pude marcar la ruto. Preparate, se pone más frío cuanto más bajes y"
" parece que los archivos estaban en el cuarto nivel del sótano."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Kill Bandits"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
msgid "Have you completed your mission?"
msgstr "¿Ya completaste la misión?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
msgid "Heard anything about the outside world?"
msgstr "¿Escuchaste algo del mundo exterior?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "I have the money, let's get started."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgctxt "npc:f"
msgid ""
"I'm a doctor, one of the several at the outpost.  We were the lucky ones.  "
"Came here right went things started to go wrong, never left."
msgstr ""
"Soy médico, uno de los varios que hay en el campamento. Somos los que "
"tuvimos suerte. Vinimos acá justo cuando las cosas empezaron a ir mal, nunca"
" nos fuimos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgctxt "npc:m"
msgid ""
"I'm a doctor, one of the several at the outpost.  We were the lucky ones.  "
"Came here right went things started to go wrong, never left."
msgstr ""
"Soy médico, uno de los varios que hay en el campamento. Somos los que "
"tuvimos suerte. Vinimos acá justo cuando las cosas empezaron a ir mal, nunca"
" nos fuimos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#. ~ You don't need to translate genders that aren't in your language
#. ~ Check: https://github.com/Cataclysm-TLG/Cataclysm-
#. TLG/blob/master/doc/TRANSLATING.md#grammatical-gender
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgctxt "npc:n"
msgid ""
"I'm a doctor, one of the several at the outpost.  We were the lucky ones.  "
"Came here right went things started to go wrong, never left."
msgstr ""
"Soy médico, uno de los varios que hay en el campamento. Somos los que "
"tuvimos suerte. Vinimos acá justo cuando las cosas empezaron a ir mal, nunca"
" nos fuimos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"I'm not exactly turning a profit back here.  That money's going toward "
"paying for more supplies so I can keep doing my job, and those supplies come"
" from people like you, who expect to be paid for risking life and limb for "
"bringing them here.  If you can't pay, then I'm sorry, but we are in the "
"middle of an unprecedented calamity.  We should all thank heaven that we're "
"still breathing at all."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"If the laboratory is locked, maybe you can find an id card from employees "
"who died in the evacuation.  Also brush up on your computer skills, any "
"computers will have some security on them.  Bring back anything you find on "
"a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"Si el laboratorio está cerrado, tal vez puedas encontrar una tarjeta de "
"identificación de algún empleado que haya muerto en la evacuación. También "
"andá con tus habilidades informáticas a punto, cualquier computadora va a "
"tener seguridad alta. Traete un pendrive con toda la información que "
"consigas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"In the data we found a major contract for tunneling and train equipment, "
"ordered four years before things went to hell.  It's the best lead we have."
"  Here's the address of the government lab where the equipment was "
"delivered.  I want you to go there, find the tunnels that they dug, and "
"download everything you can about the train network.  On the other hand, our"
" sponsors were extremely impressed in getting this far without their "
"direction, and would like to apologize by supporting this mission with a "
"whole 300 merch!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Necrosis?  It didn't detect a novel pathogen?  Maybe there's something else "
"here we can use…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
#: data/mods/Sky_Island/dialog_statue.json
msgid "Nevermind…"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Sightings of unusual living dead or new mutations.  The more we know about "
"what's happening, the closer we can get to a treatment or maybe even a cure."
"  It's a long shot, but you have hope to survive."
msgstr ""
"Que hayan visto algún muerto viviente inusual o mutaciones nuevas. Mientras "
"más sepamos de lo que pasa, más cerca estamos de conseguir un tratamiento o "
"tal vez una cura. Es poco probable, pero hay que tener esperanza."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "So glad for your help."
msgstr "Te agradezco que nos ayudes."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"So there looks to be months, maybe years of experiments, and that data set "
"must be huge.  Database servers massive enough to house it would overheat "
"running on emergency power.  But I did find communications from a lab that "
"had some kind of freezing portal open during the Cataclysm, sending "
"everything to subzero temperatures.  I bet the archives inside that lab are "
"still working.  The Old Guard didn't seem very convinced, but still ended up"
" providing 100 merch for this."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "So what are you doing right now?"
msgstr "Así que, ¿qué andás haciendo?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Supplies are stretched thin and you're not a resident here, but I could "
"provide you with wound care and a physical for fifteen merch."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Thanks!  This data looks damaged, but maybe I can make something out of it."
msgstr ""
"¡Gracias! Esta información parece dañada, pero tal vez pueda recuperar algo."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "Thanks!  This is a lot of data to go through."
msgstr "¡Gracias! Aunque esto es muchísima información para analizar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Research Archives"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"That lab is going to start freezing and just get colder the deeper you go.  "
"You'll really need special equipment to survive that far down.  Bring back "
"anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"Ese laboratorio va a empezar a congelarse y cada vez más frío mientras más "
"bajes. Vas a necesitar equipamiento especial para sobrevivir ahí abajo. Traé"
" todo lo que encontrés en un pendrive."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "That's a little expensive."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"The Old Guard--that's what's left of the feds--set me up here to screen any "
"new arrivals for infection risks.  Can't be too paranoid these days.  Sad to"
" have to turn people away, but I like the assignment for the chance to get "
"news about the outside world."
msgstr ""
"La Vieja Guardia--eso es lo que quedó de los federales--me dejaron para "
"proteger a los nuevos de cualquier riesgo de infección. No se puede ser muy "
"paranoico en estos tiempos. Me da lástima tener que rechazar a algunos, pero"
" me gusta el trabajo porque puedo enterarme de las noticias del mundo "
"exterior."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Find Lab Tunnels"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"The equipment was rated for 50 feet underground, so that tunnel entrance is "
"going to be deeper inside a lab than a normal subway.  Fifty feet would mean"
" maybe four stories down.  Bring back anything you find on a USB drive."
msgstr ""
"El equipamiento fue clasificado para 15 metros bajo tierra, así que la "
"entrada del túnel va a estar más abajo que una entrada normal de subte, "
"debajo del laboratorio. Quince metros son unos cuatro pisos para abajo. "
"Traete en un pendrive toda la información que encontrés."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"This isn't like in the movies.  The dead seem to be getting stronger as the "
"days go on.  Some survivors too, come in here with… adaptations.  Maybe "
"they're related."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Unfortunately the data you got was incomplete and mostly encrypted.  There "
"may be a way to get encryption codes, though.  I found a complaint by the "
"infosec team that they were unable to deliver critical security updates to "
"one research site.  It was some kind of more restricted secondary site "
"hidden beneath a town, they weren't allowed in.  That means it should have "
"unsecured computers we can get the codes from.  I couldn't secure any "
"funding for this due to a lack of obvious results, but if you believe in "
"this enough, maybe we can convince them otherwise?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"We don't have spare medicine to sell, if that's what you're asking.  If "
"you've got extra supplies and you want to be paid for them, go talk to "
"Smokes at the other window, he'll get you all sorted out."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Analyze Zombie Blood"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"We don't have the equipment for real analysis here so it'll need to be done "
"in the field.  I need you to get a fresh sample of zombie blood, take it to "
"a hospital, and perform a centrifuge analysis of it.  I've been authorized "
"to reward the completion of this job with 30 merch, a sizeable sum of the "
"local currency."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid "What kind of news?"
msgstr "¿Qué clase de noticias?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Workstation Data"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"When you analyzed that blood, the computer didn't pick up any virus or "
"parasite that could be causing this, but something weird happened.  The "
"computer you used triggered a government alert.  Medical staff was under "
"orders to immediately drive any matching samples to the nearest laboratory."
"  That must mean the government knew!  We have the destination address.  Go "
"there, get in, and bring back any records you can download off a computer.  "
"Like last time, I can compensate you, and the Old Guard saw enough promise "
"in this assignment to spare a larger sum of 60 merch.  I'm sure you're also "
"free to lay claim to any valuables you might find at the target location."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Download Encryption Codes"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/NPC_old_guard_doctor.json
msgid ""
"Wonderful!  Now I just need to get an undamaged, complete archive, and we "
"can really figure out what happened."
msgstr ""
"¡Maravilloso! Ahora solamente necesito encontrar un archivo completo, sin "
"daños, y podemos descubrir lo que pasó."

#. ~ Unique name of a male NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as shopkeeper with missions.  Faction
#. critical.  Real name: Gavin Wheeler
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/NPC_Smokes.json
msgid "Smokes"
msgstr "Smokes"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"*looks at you cautiously.  \"He hasn't been bothering you, has he?  Dave's "
"usually pretty harmless.\""
msgstr ""
"*te mira cautelosamente. \"No te estuvo molestando, ¿no? Usualmente, Dave es"
" bastante inofensivo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"*rubs his chin.  \"It's probably technically a fire hazard, but there's not "
"much to light up there besides what Dave brings.  And a few of the guards "
"are pretty attached to him, so we could maybe send folks up to keep an eye "
"on him and make sure he's doing okay.  That wouldn't interfere with comings "
"and goings, either.\"  He pauses a moment, looking at his ledger as if it "
"contains answers.  \"You know what?  Sure.  If Dave is okay with it, I can "
"talk the others into letting him have rooftop access to build himself a "
"little shelter, as long as he continues to keep it clean up there like he "
"has in here.\""
msgstr ""
"*se frota la pera. \"Es técnicamente un riesgo de incendio pero no hay mucho"
" para quemar ahí más allá de lo que traiga Dave. Y algunos guardias están "
"encariñados con él así que tal vez podríamos mandar algunos a cuidarlo y "
"asegurarse que esté bien. Eso no va a interferir con las llegadas y salidas,"
" tampoco.\" Se queda callado por un momento, mirando sus libros de "
"contabilidad como si ahí estuviera la respuesta. \"¿Sabés qué? Dale. Si a "
"Dave le parece bien, puedo hablar con los otros para dejarle el acceso al "
"techo para que construya ahí un pequeño refugio, siempre y cuando lo "
"mantenga limpio.\""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Actually, I can see why you haven't done it yet.  Hold that thought for now."
msgstr ""
"En realidad, entiendo por qué no lo hicieron todavía. Quedate con esa idea "
"por ahora."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"At least you came back alive.  Don't sweat it too much - it's no skin off my"
" back.  If they want it that bad, they can come get another copy themselves."
msgstr ""
"Por lo menos, volviste vivo. No te preocupes mucho - no es asunto mío. Si lo"
" quieren tanto, pueden venir ellos mismos a buscar otra copia."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Clear Back Bay"
msgstr "Limpiar Plataforma de Atrás"

#. ~ Description of mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Clear out the barricaded back area in the refugee center and lay the former "
"leader of the Free Merchants to rest, in exchange for the local currency: "
"Free Merchant certified notes."
msgstr ""
"Limpiar la parte barricada de atrás del centro de refugiados y eliminar al "
"antiguo líder de los Mercaderes Libres, a cambio de la moneda local: Bonos "
"Certificados de los Mercaderes Libres."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Secure Trade Route"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_old_guard_representative.json
msgid ""
"Come back when you get a chance, we really need to start reclaiming the "
"region."
msgstr ""
"Volvé cuando tengas la oportunidad, realmente necesitamos empezar a "
"recuperar la región."

#. ~ Description of mission "Solar Power"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Deliver 10 solar panel arrays to help the Free Merchants set up a renewable "
"power grid, in exchange for a handsome reward."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Deliver 100 0.5 L glass jars to the Free Merchants to kickstart their food "
"storage plans."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description of mission "Unknown Recipient"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Deliver the FEMA hard drive to the strange group that Smokes mentioned.  "
"Return to the evacuation center when the data's been delivered."
msgstr ""
"Llevar el disco rígido de FEMA al grupo de extraños que mencionó Smokes. "
"Volver al centro de evacuación cuando la información haya sido entregada."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Do you have the prospectus?"
msgstr "¿Tenés el informe?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Don't worry, I'll be careful.  I'll let you know when it's done."
msgstr "No te preocupes, voy a tener cuidado. Te aviso cuando lo haya hecho."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Forget I said anything."
msgstr "Olvidate de lo que dije."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Got the hard drive delivered?"
msgstr "¿Ya entregaste el disco rígido?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Great, I know it isn't much but we hope to continue to expand thanks to your"
" help."
msgstr ""
"Buenísimo, sé que no es mucho pero esperamos continuar expandiendo gracias a"
" tu ayuda."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"He wants permission to build himself a little shelter outside of your lobby,"
" somewhere out of the way.  He'd need access to your washrooms and things, "
"but you could clear him out of this space."
msgstr ""
"Quiere permiso para construirse un pequeño refugio afuera del hall, en algún"
" lugar que no moleste. Va a necesitar acceso a los baños y cosas pero "
"podrías sacarlo de este lugar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Hmm.\"  Smokes looks thoughtful, rubbing his chin.  \"Well, most of the "
"people downstairs aren't willing to come up for things like that, and a lot "
"of folks that are up here have a lot of bad memories from that.  You could "
"try asking around some of the people we have upstairs, but it'll be tough.  "
"If you have some merch you could spare, though, I could get some people off "
"guard duty and into your little crew for some hazard pay.  You might also "
"have luck asking the Old Guard rep in the southwest bay, near the library - "
"I hear they've got some volunteers lately."
msgstr ""
"Hmm.\" Smokes parece pensativo, acariciándose la pera. \"Bueno, la mayoría "
"de la gente de abajo no quieren subir por cosas como esa, y muchos de los "
"que están acá arriba tienen muchos recuerdos malos de eso. Podrías intentar "
"preguntarle a algunos de los de arriba pero va a ser difícil. Si tenés unos "
"mercs podrías contratar a algunos guardias por un precio acorde al riesgo. "
"También podrías tener suerte preguntándole al representante de la Vieja "
"Guardia en la bahía suroeste, cerca de la biblioteca - me dijeron que tienen"
" unos voluntarios."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"I could share the dropoff location if you want to bring the drive there for "
"us, but whatever's there, I'm not sure it's worth all the trouble.  I'll "
"reward you for your trouble."
msgstr ""
"Te puedo decir la ubicación para la entrega si querés llevar el disco por "
"nosotros pero lo que sea que haya ahí, no te puedo asegurar que valga la "
"pena. Yo te voy a recompensar el esfuerzo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"I was hoping you'd say that.  It's an old isolated building not too far from"
" here; you should probably just leave the drive to whoever's there and be on"
" your way.  And like I said, be careful approaching the place.  I wouldn't "
"like leading you straight into your death."
msgstr ""
"Estaba esperando que dijeras eso. Es un viejo edificio aislado que no está "
"muy lejos de acá, probablemente tengas que dejarle el disco a quien sea que "
"esté ahí e irte. Y como dije, tené cuidado cuando te acerques al lugar. No "
"me gustaría guiarte derechito a tu muerte."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "I'm sure I'll manage."
msgstr "Estoy seguro que lo voy a poder manejar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "I'm sure the outpost will expand quickly with your assistance."
msgstr "Estoy seguro que el puesto se va a expandir rápidamente con tu ayuda."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "If you can do this for us our survival options would vastly increase."
msgstr ""
"Si podés hacer esto por nosotros, nuestras opciones de supervivencia se "
"verán muy incrementadas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "If you can, get a friend or two to help you."
msgstr "Si podés, conseguite un amigo o dos para que te ayuden."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"If you really want to lend a hand we could use your help clearing out the "
"dead in the back bay.  Fearful of going outside during the first days of the"
" Cataclysm we ended up throwing our dead and the zombies we managed to kill "
"in the sealed back bay.  Our promising leader at the time even fell… he "
"turned into something different.  Kill all of them and make sure they won't "
"bother us again.  We can't pay much, besides some of our own internal money "
"which isn't good for that much yet, but it would help us to reclaim the bay."
"  <color_red>If you accept, I'll tell the guards to immediately take down "
"the barricade in the back.  You should only accept if you're ready to do "
"this now.</color>"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "In a Pickle"
msgstr "En un Berenjenal"

#. ~ Description of mission "Missing Caravan"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Investigate the last known location of a disappeared scavenger trading "
"party, and eliminate any bandits or raiders in the vicinity in exchange for "
"<reward_count:FMCNote> certified notes."
msgstr ""
"Investigar el último lugar conocido del grupo de cartoneros desaparecido, y "
"eliminar los bandidos o saqueadores en los alrededores a cambio de "
"<reward_count:FMCNote> Bonos Certificados."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"It'll take a load off my shoulders if I can finally stop worrying about "
"this."
msgstr ""
"Me vas a sacar un peso de encima si puedo dejar de preocuparme por esto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Just follow your map."
msgstr "Solo seguí tu mapa."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Missing Caravan"
msgstr "Caravana Perdida"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Unknown Recipient"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Oh, good.  I'm glad you're alright; I had no idea what to make of them.  "
"Well, one less thing to worry about."
msgstr ""
"Ah, bien. Me alegra que estés bien; no tenía idea qué hacer con ellos. "
"Bueno, una cosa menos para preocuparse."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Our community survives on trade, we appreciate it."
msgstr "Nuestra comunidad sobrevive gracias al comercio, lo apreciamos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Please be careful, we don't need any more deaths."
msgstr "Por favor tené cuidado, no queremos más muertos."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Retrieve Prospectus"
msgstr "Recuperar Informe"

#. ~ Name of the monster group "GROUP_REFUGEE_BOSS_ZOMBIE" placed on map
#. update on start of mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Sean McLaughlin"
msgstr "Sean McLaughlin"

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Solar Power"
msgstr "Energía Solar"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Solar panel arrays are pretty common on solar farms and on rooftops."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Sure, sounds great on paper, but *where*?  We aren't swimming in real estate"
" here, the place is seriously overcrowded.  And I won't have him living out "
"of a soggy cardboard box on the doorstep, it's an even worse look than the "
"lobby."
msgstr ""
"Seguro, parece genial en los papeles pero ¿*dónde*? No estamos inundados de "
"lugares libres por acá, está todo superpoblado. Y no quiero que esté "
"viviendo en una caja de cartón mojado en una puerta, es peor que el hall."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Thank you very much!"
msgstr "¡Muchas gracias!"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you, having that big of a threat close to home was nerve wracking.  "
"Here's some of our local certified notes, we've been paying these to our "
"workers in exchange for supplies.  They're getting some value in the center "
"as a trade item, I'm afraid they're all we have to spare at the moment."
msgstr ""
"Gracias, tener esa amenaza tan grande cerca de casa es estresante. Acá tenés"
" algunos bonos certificados locales, con esto le pagamos a nuestros "
"trabajadores a cambio de suministros. Tienen algo de valor en el centro como"
" objeto de cambio, pero es lo único que tenemos para darte por el momento."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Thank you, the world is a better place without them.  Two of our more "
"skilled individuals accepted the assistance of the Old Guard in setting up "
"an outpost while you were out.  We didn't have many other options, refugees "
"are still streaming in and we don't know what else to do with our limited "
"food supply.  If you get a chance, you should see if they need your "
"assistance in the future…"
msgstr ""
"Gracias, el mundo es un lugar mejor sin ellos. Dos de nuestros mejores "
"hombres han aceptado la ayuda de la Vieja Guardia para establecer un puesto "
"mientras vos no estabas. No teníamos otras opciones, los refugiados todavía "
"están llegando y no sabemos qué otra cosa hacer con nuestra provisión "
"limitada de comida. Si tenés la oportunidad, deberías ir a ver si necesitan "
"tu ayuda…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Thanks for the advice.  Maybe I'll come back with some more merch."
msgstr "Gracias por el consejo. Tal vez vuelva con más mercs."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Thanks.  I'll go let him know."
msgstr "Gracias. Le voy a avisar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "That seems fine to me.  I'll take your drive for you."
msgstr "Me parece bien. Voy a llevar el disco por ustedes."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"That's enough to get someone off guard duty, yeah.  Hand it here and I'll "
"set it up.\"  The money exchanges hands.  \"Right.  I haven't updated this "
"list in a while, so some people are still assigned to watch the back bay, "
"which is technically a free shift now.  I'll let one of them know about "
"what's up and they can spend the time helping to clean up back there.  Hope "
"it helps."
msgstr ""
"Eso es suficiente para sacar a un guardia del servicio, sí. Damelo a mí y yo"
" lo arreglo.\" La plata cambia de manos. \"Bien. Hace rato que no actualizo "
"esta lista así que algunos todavía están asignados a cuidar la bahía de "
"atrás, que técnicamente es un turno libre ahora. Le voy a decir a uno de "
"ellos y puede pasar tiempo ayudando a limpiar allá. Espero que ayude."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"That's one less thing to worry about.  Glad to have someone like you on our "
"side.  Here's 25 merch, and the broker will buy any further glass jars you "
"can find - at a reduced price, we can't keep up the premium rate.  Actually,"
" the broker was saying they had some jobs like this for you, and that it "
"might be easier to just go straight through their office if you want more "
"work."
msgstr ""
"Una cosa menos en qué preocuparse. Me alegra tener a alguien como vos de mi "
"lado. Acá tenés 25 mercs, y el comerciante va a comprar cualquier otro "
"frasco de vidrio que traigas - a un precio reducido, no podemos seguir "
"pagándote tanto. En realidad, el agente dice que tiene otros trabajos como "
"este para vos, y que puede ser más fácil ir directamente a su oficina si "
"buscás más trabajo."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"The doctor paid us in advance to get some old FEMA info from our computers "
"here, and told us to deliver the data to an isolated building afterwards.  "
"We still haven't done that.  I'm half worried it might have been some kind "
"of trap, or trick."
msgstr ""
"El médico nos pagó por adelantado para recibir información sobre FEMA de "
"nuestra computadoras, y nos dijo que lleváramos la información a un edificio"
" aislado. Todavía no lo hicimos eso. Estoy un poco preocupado de que sea "
"algún tipo de trampa o truco."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Missing Caravan"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"This is a bit more involved than the last request, we recently lost a "
"scavenger party coming to trade with us and would like you to investigate.  "
"We strongly suspect a raider band or horde caught them off-guard.  I can "
"give you the coordinates of their last radio message but little else.  In "
"either case, deal with the threat so that the scavengers can continue to "
"pass through in relative safety.  The best reward I can offer is a claim to "
"the supplies they were carrying, plus thirty certified notes - that's our "
"own internal money, good for trading and such."
msgstr ""
"Esta es un poco más complicada que la última tarea, recientemente perdimos "
"un grupo de cartoneros que venían a comerciar con nosotros y nos gustaría "
"que investigues. Sospechamos que una banda de saqueadores o una horda los "
"agarró desprevenidos. Te puedo dar las coordenadas del último mensaje de "
"radio pero nada más. En cualquier caso, encargate de la amenaza así los "
"cartoneros pueden seguir pasando relativamente seguros. La mejor recompensa "
"que te puedo ofrecer es que te quedes con los suministros que ellos llevaban"
" además de treinta bonos certificados - que es nuestra moneda interna, sirve"
" para comerciar y esas cosas."

#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Unknown Recipient"
msgstr "Recipiente Desconocido"

#. ~ Description of mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Visit the farming commune and bring the foreman's prospectus back to the "
"refugee center, for <reward_count:FMCNote> certified notes."
msgstr ""
"Visitar la comunidad granjera y traer el informe del capataz de nuevo al "
"centro de refugiados, por <reward_count:FMCNote> bonos certificados."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Solar Power"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"We are starting to build new infrastructure here and would like to get a few"
" new electrical systems online… unfortunately our existing system relies on "
"an array of something called RTGs.  Running generators isn't a viable option"
" underground, of course.  We have a big flat roof up top, and if we had a "
"few solar panel arrays we could use them to top up our usage.  We could pay "
"you pretty handsomely to bring us, say, ten solar panel arrays?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"We recently set out some skilled people to start an outpost, to secure us "
"some food supplies in a safer location.  The new outpost that we've started "
"could use your assistance.  I need you to get the foreman's prospectus "
"before we begin to send additional refugees to the farming commune.  Consult"
" with the foreman to get more detailed tasks.  We've got 50 Certified Notes "
"for you if you can do this for us."
msgstr ""
"Recientemente, mandamos unas personas a iniciar un puesto, para asegurarnos "
"comida en un lugar más seguro. El nuevo puesto que hemos comenzado podría "
"usar tu ayuda. Necesito que consigas el informe del capataz antes de empezar"
" a mandar más refugiados a la comunidad de la granja. Preguntale al capataz "
"para obtener tareas más detalladas. Tenemos 50 Bonos Certificados para darte"
" si podés hacer esto."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"We'll hold for the moment, but I'll get an ulcer if I have to keep worrying."
"  If you reconsider let me know."
msgstr ""
"Vamos a esperar por el momento, pero me va a salir una úlcera si me sigo "
"preocupando. Avisame si lo volvés a considerar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Well, we had an odd group come by maybe two days after the power grid went "
"off.  Two armed guards wearing brown uniforms, and what looked like a "
"government doctor, had a hazmat suit on.  Everyone had masks they never took"
" off.  They looked organized… maybe a military remnant from somewhere close "
"by."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, vino un grupo extraño unos dos días después de que se cortó la red "
"eléctrica. Dos guardias armados con uniformes marrones y lo que parecía un "
"doctor del gobierno, tenía un traje NBQ puesto. Todos tenían máscaras que "
"nunca se sacaron. Se los veía organizados… tal vez un remanente militar de "
"algún lugar cercano."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"What about the rooftop?  There's a stair access there, I can see it from "
"outside, and he'd probably be able to do a bit of a lookout job."
msgstr ""
"¿Y qué te parece el techo? Hay una escalera que va arriba, puedo verla desde"
" afuera y probablemente pueda hacer un poco de trabajo de guardia desde ahí."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "What were they here for?"
msgstr "¿Y para qué vinieron?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Where's that building at, exactly?"
msgstr "¿Dónde está exactamente ese edificio?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "In a Pickle"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"While we've managed to secure day to day food supplies, it's very much hand "
"to mouth.  Our reserves would barely last a few days if something kept our "
"people locked in.  We need a stockpile to avoid that.  Thanks to our outpost"
" we have a bit of meat and vegetables coming in, but we need a better way to"
" preserve them.  Some of our people know enough about food canning that if "
"we had a good stock of canning jars, we could make pickles and canned meats "
"to get us set for the winter.  I'll pay you a premium rate if you can bring "
"us around a hundred jars to get us started."
msgstr ""
"Mientras nos pudimos asegurar la comida para el día a día, llegamos con lo "
"justo. Nuestras reservas apenas alcanzarán para unos días si algo hace que "
"nos tengamos que mantener encerrados. Necesitamos suministros para evitar "
"eso. Gracias a nuestro puesto tenemos un poco de carne y verduras llegando, "
"pero necesitamos una mejor manera para preservarlos. Algunos saben cómo "
"enlatar comidas, si tuviéramos una buena cantidad de frascos para conserva, "
"podríamos hacer pickles y carne enlatada para pasar el invierno. Te voy a "
"pagar mejor si nos podés traer unos cien frascos como para que empecemos."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Clear Back Bay"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "Will they be bothering us any longer?"
msgstr "¿Ya no nos van a moletar más?"

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Retrieve Prospectus"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"With this we'll be able to convince others to invest in the commune.  Thank "
"you, here's your money.  We also managed to get a manual crank hooked up to "
"the garage in the back, so feel free to make use of that - you've been a "
"great help to us."
msgstr ""
"Con esto seremos capaces de convencer a otros de invertir en nuestra "
"comunidad. Gracias, acá está tu plata. También pudimos conseguir una palanca"
" para conectar en el garage en la parte de atrás, así que usalo cuando "
"quieras - fuiste de gran ayuda para nosotros."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid ""
"Woah, you're really intent, hey?  That's a lot for most people here.\"  The "
"money exchanges hands.  \"That's enough to get two people off guard duty for"
" an afternoon, even with all the ugliness back there.  And you know what?  "
"I'll help out, too, so make that three.  I can appreciate someone who's "
"willing to put their money where their mouth is."
msgstr ""
"Wow, estás verdaderamente decidido, ¿eh? Eso es más que la mayoría de gente "
"de acá.\" La plata cambia de manos. \"Eso es suficiente para conseguir que "
"dos personas dejen la guardia por una tarde, incluso con toda la porquería "
"de allá atrás. ¿Y sabés qué? Yo también voy a ayudar, así que tres. Puedo "
"apreciar a alguien que está decidido a poner su plata donde pone sus "
"palabras."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "You seem right to be suspicious."
msgstr "Tenés razón en sospechar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "[10 merch] How about ten merch to do it?"
msgstr "[10 mercs] ¿Diez mercs te parecen suficientes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_missions.json
msgid "[5 merch] Five merch for someone sounds fair to me."
msgstr "[5 mercs] Cinco mercs por alguien me parece bien."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "'Sorry, we're full'?  Do you greet everyone like that?"
msgstr "'¿Perdón, estamos llenos'? ¿A todos los recibís así?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"*waves you over.  \"I haven't seen you before.  Welcome to our little homely"
" house.\""
msgstr ""
"*te saluda con la mano. \"No te había visto antes. Bienvenido a nuestra "
"pequeña casita.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Alright, shoot."
msgstr "Bueno, decime."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"And so we did.\"  Smokes reaches under their table, counts out some money, "
"and slides it through a slot in the glass.  \"Here's five merch a head for "
"the folks you found a new home for.  We won't forget it"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"And so we did.\"  Smokes reaches under their table, counts out some money, "
"and slides it through a slot in the glass.  \"Here's five merch a head for "
"the folks you found a new home for.  We won't forget it."
msgstr ""
"Y lo hicimos.\" Smokes busca abajo de la mesa, cuenta un poco de plata y la "
"pasa por una ranura en el vidrio. \"Acá hay cinco mercs por cada uno al que "
"le consigas un lugar nuevo. No lo vamos a olvidar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Are you interested in any chemical supplies?"
msgstr "¿Están interesados en suministros químicos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Are you interested in any household goods?"
msgstr "¿Están interesados en artículos para el hogar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Before you ask, we're full.  You're right about the refugee part, but we're "
"way over capacity right now.  We don't have the food or space to take on "
"anyone else.\"  He softens a little.  \"As for me, I do a lot of things "
"here, but mostly I keep tabs on our supplies.  You can call me Smokes, or "
"Gavin; whichever you prefer.  I also trade with people from outside, like "
"you.  If you're in the market for hardware, we're selling, and if you have "
"food, we are very much buying.  Anyways, uh, what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""
"Antes de que preguntes, estamos llenos. Tenés razón sobre los refugiados "
"pero estamos por sobre nuestra capacidad. No tenemos ni la comida ni el "
"espacio para recibir a nadie más.\" Se tranquiliza un poco. \"Por mi parte, "
"hago muchas cosas acá pero mayormente controlo los suministros de nuestros "
"recursos. Me podés decir Smokes, o Gavin; como prefieras. También comercio "
"con gente de afuera, como vos. Si estás buscando herramientas, tenemos para "
"vender, y si tenés comida, estamos necesitando mucho. De cualquier manera, "
"¿qué puedo hacer por vos?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Best of luck."
msgstr "Te deseo la mejor de la suertes."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "But I-"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Can I talk to you about that fellow over there in the dinosaur suit?"
msgstr "¿Puedo hablar con vos sobre ese tipo ahí con el traje de dinosaurio?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Chemicals?  I'm sure we could find some use for them, and we are in need of "
"medical supplies.  What's the offer?"
msgstr ""
"¿Químicos? Seguro que les podemos encontrar alguna utilidad y necesitamos "
"suministros médicos. ¿Qué ofrecés?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Couldn't you get them out?  Your guards are well-armed."
msgstr "¿No los pudieron sacar? Sus guardias están bien armados."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Does this center need any metal?"
msgstr "¿Necesitan metal en el centro?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Give me second to write that down… okay, done."
msgstr "Esperame que escribo esto… okay, listo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Good to know."
msgstr "Es bueno saberlo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Got some time to talk?"
msgstr "¿Tenés tiempo para hablar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Hope it helps."
msgstr "Espero que sirva."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Hordes?"
msgstr "¿Hordas?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate it a lot, getting them somewhere safe.  I hope that's what you "
"did, anyway.  In any case, having the lobby clear is a big help.  Even with "
"the uh, cardboard guy still around, he's a lot easier to handle alone."
msgstr ""
"Te lo agradezco mucho, llevarlos a algún lugar seguro. Por lo menos, espero "
"que hayas hecho eso. En cualquier caso, tener el hall limpio nos ayuda "
"mucho. Incluso con el, eh, tipo del cartón todavía por acá, él solo es mucho"
" más fácil de manejar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I do believe we discussed a reward?"
msgstr "Creo que tenemos una recompensa que discutir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"I don't know, why don't you ask them?  I haven't pried, but where else do "
"they have to go?  You've seen how bad it is out there.  We don't have the "
"space for them, but it won't kill us to give them some shelter as long as "
"they aren't too much of a drain on resources."
msgstr ""
"No sé, ¿por qué no les preguntás a ellos? No me metí a chusmear pero ¿a "
"dónde van a ir? Ya viste cómo está todo afuera. No tenemos lugar para ellos "
"pero no nos va matar darles refugio siempre y cuando no gasten nuestros "
"recursos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I don't see that many of you around."
msgstr "No veo que sean muchos ustedes."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I just wanted to look around.  See you."
msgstr "Estaba mirando nada más. Hasta luego."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I took care of your beggar problem."
msgstr "Te resolví el problema con los mendigos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I'll see what I can do.  What's merch?"
msgstr "Voy a ver qué puedo hacer. ¿Qué es un merc?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "I'm looking for work.  Can I do anything for the center?"
msgstr "Estoy buscando trabajo. ¿Hay algo que pueda hacer para el centro?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Jesus, man, we aren't monsters.  I'm sure we could get them out if we really"
" needed to, yeah, but why would we do that?  We need to be stringent with "
"who we take on, that's true, but forcing out people in need isn't a great "
"way to convince anyone that we're reliable allies.  The world doesn't run on"
" good faith, but it's damn well nicer to live in because of it."
msgstr ""
"Dios, chabón, no somos monstruos. Estoy seguro que podríamos echarlos si "
"necesitáramos hacerlo, sí, pero ¿por qué vamos a hacer eso? Necesitamos ser "
"estrictos sobre a quién dejamos entrar, es verdad, pero forzar a que se vaya"
" gente necesitada no es una buena manera de convencer a nadie que somos "
"aliados confiables. El mundo no funciona con buena fe pero sigue siendo "
"mejor vivir por ella."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Just glad to help."
msgstr "Me alegra poder ayudar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Lay it on me."
msgstr "Dejámelo a mí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Listen, buddy.  We were putting away some of the last food you gave us and "
"noticed it was… off.  Okay I'll cut the shit- It was people.  I don't know "
"how you got it, or what you did, but we aren't taking any chances.  You are "
"not welcome here anymore.  <color_red>I'll give you one minute</color> to "
"fuck off and never come back."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Mind if I take a look at your stock?"
msgstr "¿Te molesta si miro el suministro que tienen?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Next shipment should arrive in around <interval>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "No guarantees, but I'll see what I can do."
msgstr "No garantizo nada pero voy a ver qué puedo hacer."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"No, unfortunately.  They're folks that wanted to join us, but we're too full"
" and we don't have enough to share.  Most people leave and look for their "
"own place when we turn them down, but these ones… didn't.  We've been trying"
" to find them a safe place, but there's a shortage of those these days, for "
"reasons I'm sure you can guess.  Until then, we're letting them crash here "
"as long as they don't mess the place up."
msgstr ""
"Lamentablemente, no. Había gente que se quería unir pero estamos llenos y no"
" tenemos suficientes cosas para compartir. La mayoría de la gente se fue y "
"buscó su propio lugar cuando empezamos a rechazarlos pero estos… no se "
"fueron. Intentamos encontrarles un lugar seguro pero hay muy pocos de esos "
"por estos días, por razones que creo que ya conoces. Hasta entonces, estamos"
" dejando que se queden acá siempre y cuando no molesten."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Not as much as I'd like, I'm afraid.  Most of these shelters seemed to have "
"been designed to make people *feel* safer, not to actually keep them safe.  "
"Our radio equipment is terrible… I don't think it was even meant to be used "
"seriously.  I've heard some talk of hordes."
msgstr ""
"No tanto como me gustaría, lamentablemente. La mayoría de estos refugios "
"parecen haber sido diseñados para hacer que la gente *se sienta* segura, "
"pero no para que esté verdaderamente segura. Nuestro equipo de radio es "
"terrible… No creo que haya sido hecho para ser usado. Escuché algunas "
"conversaciones sobre hordas."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Radios?  That seems awfully specific."
msgstr "¿Radios? Eso parece extremadamente específico."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Something on your mind?"
msgstr "¿Tenés algo en mente?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Stick around for <interval>, there will surely be something you'd like."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Sure, we could use some around here for repairs and whatnot.  What are the "
"terms?"
msgstr ""
"Seguro, podemos necesitar algunas para reparaciones y cosas así. ¿Qué "
"términos ofrecés?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Thanks, I will make sure to check back.  Farewell."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Tools, to be precise.  The basement and the storage rooms had way more than "
"we need, and a lot of people brought their own when they were evacuating.  "
"There's more than we could ever use, so we'll be happy to sell them at a "
"very fair price.  Nothing in the way of radios, so you'll have to look "
"somewhere else for that."
msgstr ""
"Herramientas, más precisamente. El sótano y las habitaciones de "
"almacenamiento tienen mucho más de lo que necesitamos, y mucha gente trajo "
"sus propias cosas en la evacuación. Hay más de lo que vamos a usar así que "
"con gusto podemos venderlas por un precio justo. Pero nada de radios, eso lo"
" vas a tener que buscar en otro lugar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Wait, basement?  I didn't know this place had a basement."
msgstr "Esperá, ¿sótano? No sabía que este lugar tenía un sótano."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"We are running a bit short on toilet paper, soap, toothpaste…  What's the "
"offer?"
msgstr ""
"Nos estamos quedando sin papel higiénico, jabón, dentífrico… ¿Qué ofrecés?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"We've had some issues with scavengers.  Apparently a big part of the "
"marketing for these shelters was high-end radio equipment that they could "
"use to keep in touch with each other, and a lot of the people we've traded "
"with have asked about it.  Not that we don't have any radios, mind you, but "
"they're all absolutely awful.  Even if we *could* spare any, they'd be "
"useless to anyone that actually needed it - not much point in lugging around"
" a ham radio that can't pick up anything more than a mile away."
msgstr ""
"Tuvimos algunos problemas con cartoneros. Aparentemente, un parte de la "
"publicidad de estos refugios era el equipo de radio que se podría usar para "
"comunicarse con los demás, y mucha gente con la que comerciamos nos "
"preguntaron por eso. No es que no tengamos radios, eso sí, pero son "
"espantosas. Incluso si *tuviéramos* alguna para vender, no tienen la "
"utilidad necesaria - no tiene mucho sentido llevar un equipo de radio que no"
" agarra nada a más de un kilómetro y medio."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Well, how about 200 merch for 75 pounds of…"
msgstr "Bueno, ¿qué te parece 200 mercs por 35 kilos de…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Well, how about 250 merch for 100 pounds of…"
msgstr "Bueno, ¿qué te parece 250 mercs por 45 kilos de…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Well, how about 300 merch for 10 liters of…"
msgstr "Bueno, ¿qué te parece 300 mercs por 10 litros de…"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "What's with these 'Free Merchant certified notes'?"
msgstr "¿Qué onda con estos 'bonos certificados de los Mercaderes Libres'?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "What's with these people in the lobby?  Are they with you?"
msgstr "¿Qué onda esa gente en el hall? ¿Están con ustedes?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "When will you have new stuff in stock?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Who are you?  This is a refugee center, right?"
msgstr "¿Quién sos? Esto es un centro de refugiados, ¿no?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "Why haven't they gone anywhere else?"
msgstr "¿Y por qué no se fueron a otro lado?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"Yes we are.  The center had a good stock of those awful soy bars, but "
"between all of us, it went fast.  We're making do with what we can skim off "
"the edge of towns, but mostly we rely on trade from people like you.  "
"Speaking of, we'll pay top dollar for anything preserved - canned, salted, "
"dried, whatever.  Just talk to the broker in the back."
msgstr ""
"Sí, así es. El centro tenía un bueno suministro de esas horribles barras de "
"soja pero entre nosotros, se terminaron rápido. Estamos viviendo con lo que "
"podemos agarrar de las casas en los bordes de los pueblos, pero mayormente "
"dependemos de comerciar con gente como vos. Hablando de eso, podemos pagar "
"bien por cualquier conserva - latas, salados, disecados, lo que sea. Hablá "
"con el comerciante que está atrás."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "You know where to find me."
msgstr "Ya sabés dónde encontrarme."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "You mentioned you were selling hardware?"
msgstr "¿Me dijiste que están vendiendo herramientas?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid "You're having trouble with food?"
msgstr "¿Están con problemas de comida?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk.json
msgid ""
"[Social 1] If I could look into clearing them out of here, would you be able"
" to pay me back?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"*bristles.  \"I know, alright?  I do.  I hate it too.  But we are packed to "
"the gills right now, and the only way we're going to stay alive is if we "
"keep our gates closed fast.  I don't know what made the scavengers out there"
" so ruthless, but some of us have had to kill our own kids.  Please show "
"some consideration.\""
msgstr ""
"*se molesta. \"Entiendo, ¿sabés? Lo entiendo. También lo odio. Pero estamos "
"hasta el techo en este momento y la única manera de que sobrevivamos es "
"manteniendo nuestras puertas cerradas. No sé qué hizo que los cartoneros "
"sean tan despiadados pero algunos de nosotros tuvimos que matar a nuestros "
"propios hijos. Por favor, tené un poco de consideración.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"*laughs.  \"Well, I think it's ridiculous, but I guess I don't mind it that "
"much.  I figure it's all in good fun, and people could really use the laugh "
"these days, y'know?  I'm sure they'd stop if I asked.  The helmet is like… a"
" badge of office, at this point.  You can call me Smokes if you really "
"want.\""
msgstr ""
"*se ríe. \"Bueno, creo que es ridículo pero supongo que no me importa mucho."
" Me parece que es divertido y a la gente le viene bien tener algo con qué "
"divertirse estos días, ¿viste? Estoy seguro que si se los pido dejarían de "
"decirme así. El casco es como… una placa de policía, en este momento. Me "
"podés decir Smokes si querés.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"*rolls his eyes.  \"Tell me about it.  My actual name is Gavin, which I "
"think I told you.  I used to be a firefighter, and people started "
"recognizing me because of the helmet.  Someone called me 'smokes' because of"
" it, and it stuck.  I hate it.  I've never even touched a cigarette.\""
msgstr ""
"*gira los ojos. \"Decímelo a mí. Mi verdadero nombre es Gavin, creo que ya "
"te lo dije. Antes era bombero y la gente empezó a reconocerme por el casco. "
"Alguien me llamó 'smokes' por eso y quedó. Lo odio. Nunca en mi vida toqué "
"un cigarrillo.\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "*shrugs.  \"Did you need something else?\""
msgstr "*se encoge de hombros. \"¿Necesitás algo más?\""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"A lot of the time, yes.  Our address is in the computers of most of the evac"
" shelters around here, and people keep showing up that we have to turn away."
"  It gets easier when you have something you can read off a script."
msgstr ""
"Muchas veces, sí. Nuestra dirección está en las computadoras de la mayoría "
"de los refugios de evacuación de por acá, y la gente sigue viniendo y las "
"tenemos que rechazar. Es más fácil cuando tenemos un guion para leerles."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Alright, alright, I'm sorry.  Bad joke."
msgstr "Bueno, bueno, perdón. Fue un chiste malo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Can't say I blame you."
msgstr "La verdad que no te culpo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Here's hoping it works out."
msgstr "Esperemos que funcione."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "How do I get down there?"
msgstr "¿Y cómo voy hasta ahí abajo?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "How'd you end up here?"
msgstr "¿Cómo terminaste acá?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"I appreciate the offer, I really do, but I'm sorry.  The basement is off-"
"limits to outsiders, and we're not in the market for new recruits right now."
"  Maybe once we're in a better spot there might be some room to think about "
"it, but right now I can't justify just giving you free reign down there."
msgstr ""
"Te agradezco la oferta, en serio, pero lo lamento. El sótanos está prohibido"
" para los de afuera, y no estamos buscando reclutar gente nueva en este "
"momento. Tal vez cuando estemos en una mejor situación podríamos pensarlo "
"pero ahora no puedo justificar darte rienda suelta ahí abajo."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "I can pull my own weight!"
msgstr "¡Puedo levantar mi propio peso!"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"I can't share that.  We're taking security extremely seriously right now.  "
"The guards downstairs are well-armed, and they've got orders to immediately "
"apprehend anyone they don't recognize.  We want to keep those people as safe"
" we can until either we have more space up here or we've got some room "
"inside the fence for them to live."
msgstr ""
"No te puedo decir. Nos tomamos la seguridad con extremo cuidado en este "
"momento. Los guardias de abajo están bien armados y tienen órdenes de "
"agarrar inmediatamente a cualquier que no reconozcan. Queremos mantener a "
"salvo a esa gente hasta que tengamos más lugar acá arriba o espacio adentro "
"de la valla para que puedan vivir."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"I can't tell if you're joking or not, but that is seriously fucked up, and I"
" don't want to hear another word about it.  Okay?"
msgstr ""
"No me doy cuenta si es un chiste o no pero la verdad que es una locura y no "
"quiero volver a escuchar algo así. ¿Estamos?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"I don't think we have a figurehead right now, I think?  If we do, I don't "
"know about it.  For the most part, we all have our own responsibilities and "
"that works to keep us all fed as a group.  I'm the front man for outsiders, "
"the broker keeps tabs on our food, so on and so forth.  We've had some town "
"hall style talks in the cafeteria about setting up a democracy, but there's "
"nothing solid on that right now."
msgstr ""
"Me parece que no tenemos un líder en este momento, creo. Si lo tenemos, no "
"sé quién es. Generalmente, todos tenemos nuestras propias responsabilidades "
"y eso funciona para mantenernos alimentados como grupo. Soy el que atiende a"
" los de afuera, el comerciante mantiene las cuentas de nuestra comida, y así"
" con todos. Tuvimos algunas reuniones en la cafetería acerca de establecer "
"una democracia pero no hay nada sólida en ese aspecto por ahora."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "I suppose that makes sense."
msgstr "Supongo que eso tiene sentido."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "I'm saying you're giving up a potential source of meat."
msgstr "Lo que digo es que estás rechazando una potencial fuente de carne."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but the last thing we need is another mouth to feed.  Most of us "
"lack any real survival skills, so keeping our group small enough to survive "
"on the food we trade for is the main thing keeping us alive."
msgstr ""
"Lo lamento pero lo último que necesitamos es otra boca para alimentar. La "
"mayoría carece de verdaderas habilidades de supervivencia, así que es "
"importante mantener un grupo pequeño para sobrevivir de la comida que "
"podemos comprar, es lo que nos mantiene vivos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"If I could go down there, I could help bring them supplies.  Food, medicine…"
msgstr ""
"Si puedo ir ahí, los puedo ayudar a conseguir suministros. Comida, "
"medicamentos…"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Just because they're not boots on the ground doesn't mean they aren't "
"helping.  In fact, I'd say that a lot of them are our most important people."
"  They keep the power running, for one thing.  And even if they weren't "
"helping, look at it this way: all of us are scared, and almost all of us "
"have lost someone from all this.  We aren't going to throw our own to the "
"wolves."
msgstr ""
"Solo porque no sean soldados no significa que no estén ayudando. De hecho, "
"diría que muchos de esos son nuestras personas más importantes. Mantienen la"
" energía funcionando, por ejemplo. E incluso si no estuvieran ayudando, "
"miralo de esta manera: todos estamos asustados y casi todos perdimos a "
"alguien en esto. No vamos a tirar a los nuestros a los lobos."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Maybe out there alone, or with a small group, but enough to feed a few dozen"
" other people that aren't helping you?  That just isn't a risk we're willing"
" to take right now.  If you want to trade us supplies or donate something, "
"you're more than welcome to, and it'd be a huge help, but right now, we're "
"far past our comfort zone as it is."
msgstr ""
"Tal vez estando solo o con un pequeño grupo pero ¿lo suficiente para "
"alimentar unas docenas de personas que no te están ayudando? Eso es un "
"riesgo que no estamos dispuestos a cometer en este momento. Si querés "
"comerciar con nosotros o donarnos algo, sos más que bienvenido y sería una "
"gran ayuda, pero en este momento estamos lejos de nuestra zona de confort."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Nevermind.  Don't know where I was going with that."
msgstr "No importa. No sé en qué estaba pensando."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"No way in hell.  I'm not going to risk the safety of dozens of people just "
"for some ass.  If you're that desperate, go talk to Alonso."
msgstr ""
"De ninguna manera. No voy a arriesgar la seguridad de docenas de personas "
"por un imbécil. Si vos estás así de desesperado, andá a hablar con Alonso."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Not much to say.  What did you want to hear?"
msgstr "No hay mucho para decir. ¿Qué querés saber?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Oh, merch.  They're just paper notes we've started using for local cash.  We"
" started out paying each other with dollar bills, but there's so much paper "
"money out there that it's just useless now.  For our internal use, we "
"started certifying bills that represent food and labor in the center here.  "
"We started trading them internally, and then they started circling around, "
"and now other people have started adopting them, too."
msgstr ""
"Oh, merc. Son unos bonos de papel que empezamos a usar como moneda local. "
"Empezamos pagándonos entre nosotros con billetes de dólar pero hay tantos "
"billetes por ahí que ya no tiene sentido. Para uso interno empezamos a "
"certificar billetes que representan el trabajo y la comida acá en el centro."
" Al principio los usábamos para comerciar internamente y después empezaron a"
" circular, así que ahora otra gente también los está usando."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Other than those people with the hard drive, none that I know of.  "
"Scavengers share some odd things, but we can't exactly go check for "
"ourselves."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Right now, it's the best way we have to make sure that everyone gets what "
"they need.  Long-term viability of business models is what people in suits "
"used to do back before all this, and we see where that got them.  Barter is "
"the only thing keeping us from starving, so we're going to keep doing it as "
"long as it works or until we can start producing our own food."
msgstr ""
"Ahora, es la mejor manera que tenemos para asegurarnos que todos tengan lo "
"que necesitan. La viabilidad a largo plazo de los modelos de negocios es lo "
"que la gente de trajes hacían antes de todo esto, y ya vemos a dónde los "
"llevó eso. El regateo es lo único que nos mantiene alejados de morir de "
"hambre, así que vamos a seguir haciéndolo mientras funcione o hasta que "
"empecemos a producir nuestra propia comida."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "Smokes?  That's quite a name."
msgstr "¿Smokes? Qué buen nombre."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "That sounds a little cruel."
msgstr "Eso parece un poco cruel."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"The center has a pretty large lower floor, behind metal doors that were made"
" to stand up to basically anything - bombs, radiation, you name it.  Place "
"is basically a vault.  Most of our population is living in there; only "
"people who we think are combat-capable stay up here.  Bear in mind, we "
"started off with a few buses of office workers and soccer moms.  If worst "
"comes to worst, they'll stand a chance if things go bad up here."
msgstr ""
"El centro tiene una planta baja bastante grande, atrás de una puertas de "
"metal que fueron hechas para aguantar casi todo - bombas, radiación, lo que "
"quieras. El lugar es básicamente una bóveda. La mayoría de nuestra población"
" está viviendo ahí; solamente la gente que creemos que es capaz de pelear se"
" queda ahí. Tené en cuenta que empezamos con unos colectivos de trabajadores"
" de oficina y amas de casa. Si sucede lo peor, van a poder defenderse si las"
" cosas llegan hasta ahí."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Things were rough at first, and our policy of taking everyone we could "
"caused a lot of strife later on.  Right now, we just want to get enough "
"trade going keep ourselves afloat.  We might have to turn people away, but "
"we've found that they're usually willing to trade with us, which is our only"
" real source of food right now.  We're trying to turn that into a business "
"model.  Doesn't matter who you are, we'll trade with you as long as you "
"don't bring trouble."
msgstr ""
"Las cosas estaban difíciles al principio y nuestra política de recibir a "
"cualquier podría habernos causado muchos conflictos en el futuro. En este "
"momento, solo queremos tener comercio suficiente como para mantenernos a "
"flote. Tal vez tengamos que rechazar gente pero usualmente quieren comerciar"
" con nosotros, que es nuestra única fuente real de comida ahora. Estamos "
"tratando de convertir eso en un modelo de negocios. No importa quién seas, "
"vamos a comerciar con vos siempre y cuando no nos causes problemas."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "We are.  That's why we're turning people away."
msgstr "Sí. Por eso estamos rechazando gente."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Well, I'm Gavin, like I said.  I was a fireman before <the_cataclysm>, and I"
" was also on duty when everything fell apart.  I'd rather not go into "
"detail, but other than that, I wasn't really much to write home about.  My "
"family was Irish, I never married, and I liked woodworking.  I volunteered "
"to take inventory of what the center had when I got off the bus, one thing "
"leads to another, and now I'm here."
msgstr ""
"Bueno, soy Gavin, como te dije. Era bombero antes del <the_cataclysm> y "
"estaba trabajando cuando todo se desmoronó. Prefiero no entrar en detalles "
"pero más allá de eso, no hay mucho más para contar. Mi familia era "
"irlandesa, nunca me casé y me gusta la carpintería. Me ofrecí como "
"voluntario para hacer inventario de lo que había en el centro cuando me bajé"
" del colectivo, una cosa llevó a la otra, y acá estoy."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "What about when the goods dry up?  Won't that happen eventually?"
msgstr ""
"¿Y qué pasa cuando se queden sin suministros? ¿No va a suceder "
"eventualmente?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Why spend so much effort keeping it locked down?  I thought you mentioned "
"they weren't able to help."
msgstr ""
"¿Para qué gastar tanto esfuerzo en mantenerlos encerrados abajo? Pensé que "
"dijiste que no eran capaces de ayudar."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid ""
"Yeah.  Someone came through this way a while back saying he had tried to "
"drive into Syracuse after the outbreak.  Didn't even make it downtown before"
" he ran into a wall of zombies that he said could stop a tank.  He "
"hightailed it out, but he said there were several thousand at least.  I "
"guess when you get a bunch of them together, they end up making enough noise"
" to attract everyone in the neighborhood.  Thankfully, we haven't had a mob "
"like that pass by here, because I'm not sure the fence would do much to keep"
" them out."
msgstr ""
"Sí, Alguien vino por acá hace un tiempo diciendo que habían intentando "
"manejar hasta Syracuse después del brote. No pudo ni salir del pueblo porque"
" se chocó con una pared de zombis que dijo que eran capaces de parar un "
"tanque. Resaltó eso pero dijo que era varios cientos por lo menos. Supongo "
"que cuando se juntan muchos, terminan haciendo tanto ruido como para atraer "
"a todos en el barrio. Por suerte, nunca pasó una horda como esa por acá "
"porque no creo que la vaya pueda hacer mucho para contenerlos."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "[Cannibal + Psychopath] Wait, I thought you were having food problems."
msgstr ""
"[Caníbal + Psicópata] Momento, pensé que tenían problemas con la comida."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_staff/Smokes/free_merchant_shopkeep_talk_fluff.json
msgid "[PER 8] If you hate it, then why are you smiling?"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Name suffix of a female NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a unique trader and potential mission
#. provider.
#. ~ Name of an NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Arsonist"
msgstr "Pirómano"

#. ~ Description of mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Bring the arsonist 120 units of commercial fertilizer"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"Commercial fertilizer tends to be made from ammonium nitrate, which is also "
"usable as an explosive.  Try looking for some around the abandoned farms."
msgstr ""
"El fertilizante comercial suele estar hecho de nitrato de amonio, que "
"también es utilizable como explosivo. Fijate alrededor de algunas granjas "
"abandonadas."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Damn.  Perhaps I wasn't the only one who thought of this."
msgstr "Mierda. Tal vez no fui el único en pensar en eso."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"Did you find any fertilizer?  Are you sure this is the ammonium nitrate "
"kind?"
msgstr ""
"¿Encontraste algo de fertilizante? ¿Estás seguro que está hecho con nitrato "
"de amonio?"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Do you have any jobs for me?"
msgstr "¿Tenés algún trabajo para mí?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"Group?  You think they'd let someone like me live here?  Nah, I'm on my own "
"and that's how I like it, I just come here to trade."
msgstr ""

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Heh, you look important."
msgstr "Parecés una persona importante."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "How are you doing these days?"
msgstr "¿Cómo la vas llevando estos días?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"I burn down buildings and sell the materials.  Nails, rebar, wire, whatever "
"metal I can pull out of the ashes."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I could use some help getting some materials."
msgstr "Me vendría bien un poco de ayuda para conseguir unos materiales."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"I could use some help getting some materials.  Molotovs are nice for burning"
" down buildings but aren't all that for keeping yourself safe.  If you could"
" get me 120 units of commercial fertilizer I could make something a lot more"
" potent."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I feel bad for asking."
msgstr "Me siento mal por preguntar."

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I guess I could convince the shelter to sell me some."
msgstr "Supongo que puedo convencer al refugio para venderme un poco."

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"I made some nice things with that ammonium nitrate you got me.  Want to "
"trade?"
msgstr ""
"Hice algunas cosas lindas con ese nitrato de amonio que me conseguiste. "
"¿Querés intercambiar?"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"I mean, there was a nuclear war and now the dead are walking, what do you "
"want me to say?  The monsters are getting bigger and weirder, and there are "
"fewer people every day.  Game over, man."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I'll buy."
msgstr "Lo voy a comprar."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I'm actually new."
msgstr "En realidad, soy nuevo."

#. ~ Job description of "Arsonist" NPC class
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "I'm just watching the world burn."
msgstr "Solo estoy observando cómo se consume el mundo."

#. ~ Unique name of a female NPC
#. ~ Appears in the refugee center as a unique trader and potential mission
#. provider.
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Makayla Sanchez"
msgstr "Makayla Sanchez"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid ""
"Nothing good.  Had a pal on the road with a ham radio, but she's gone like "
"everyone else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Nothing good?  So you have heard something"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Dialogue line in mission "Supply the arsonist"
#: data/json/npcs/refugee_center/surface_visitors/NPC_arsonist.json
msgid "Oh man, thanks so much friend.  You won't regret it."
msgstr "Uh, chabón, muchas gracias. No te vas a arrepentir."

